#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "28 new identities to earn: Bastion, Warfather, Sun Incarnate, The Unseen, Voice of Fate, Wild Sovereign, King in Bone and more - each with its own passive creed and signature skill that supersedes the last"
msgstr "28 new identities to earn: Bastion, Warfather, Sun Incarnate, The Unseen, Voice of Fate, Wild Sovereign, King in Bone and more - each with its own passive creed and signature skill that supersedes the last"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A CAT, A DOG AND TWO CHILDREN: Pixelheim has a cat that judges you, a dog that leans on you, and - once it's a village - Pip and Nell running about the square"
msgstr "A CAT, A DOG AND TWO CHILDREN: Pixelheim has a cat that judges you, a dog that leans on you, and - once it's a village - Pip and Nell running about the square"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A DAWN YOU WATCH: when Maren has the letter, the Night of Ash ends on the town itself. The camera drifts from the shrine across Pixelheim as the fires gutter out one by one and the red night greys toward morning; the survivors stand together on the square and speak in their own voices - Maren, the mayor out of his hall, Bram and Sela beside you - and when Fafnyr is named, he roars, and his shadow sweeps over the town. Then the day begins: Pixelheim, day one"
msgstr "A DAWN YOU WATCH: when Maren has the letter, the Night of Ash ends on the town itself. The camera drifts from the shrine across Pixelheim as the fires gutter out one by one and the red night greys toward morning; the survivors stand together on the square and speak in their own voices - Maren, the mayor out of his hall, Bram and Sela beside you - and when Fafnyr is named, he roars, and his shadow sweeps over the town. Then the day begins: Pixelheim, day one"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A FIFTH RANK: level 20 crowns the hero - Ironlord, Starcaller, Nightlord, Hierophant, Eldwarden, Exemplar or Deathlord - with an amethyst aura and a bonus skill point"
msgstr "A FIFTH RANK: level 20 crowns the hero - Ironlord, Starcaller, Nightlord, Hierophant, Eldwarden, Exemplar or Deathlord - with an amethyst aura and a bonus skill point"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A HOME IN THE SAME HAND: the rug, planter, bookshelf, banner, candelabra and bench you place at home are drawn like the rest of the village, the rug actually shows, and a bed's foot is the bed - rest there, but nothing can be set on it"
msgstr "A HOME IN THE SAME HAND: the rug, planter, bookshelf, banner, candelabra and bench you place at home are drawn like the rest of the village, the rug actually shows, and a bed's foot is the bed - rest there, but nothing can be set on it"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A HOME WORTH HAVING: a night in your own bed leaves you well rested (+10% XP for your next 30 fights), and furniture now helps where it stands - a bookshelf for XP, a banner for critical blows, candles for energy, a rug for gold, a plant for stronger potions, a bench for longer rest. The Manor's garden grows herbs and reeds for the cauldron"
msgstr "A HOME WORTH HAVING: a night in your own bed leaves you well rested (+10% XP for your next 30 fights), and furniture now helps where it stands - a bookshelf for XP, a banner for critical blows, candles for energy, a rug for gold, a plant for stronger potions, a bench for longer rest. The Manor's garden grows herbs and reeds for the cauldron"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A LOOT CURVE WORTH CHASING: the mountain's floors drop by how deep they are, so every band of floors is a step up - the Obsidian Blade waits on the last floors, and Dragonbane's hoard (now 23 damage) is no longer a step down. Gear drops more often, and a boss always drops a piece"
msgstr "A LOOT CURVE WORTH CHASING: the mountain's floors drop by how deep they are, so every band of floors is a step up - the Obsidian Blade waits on the last floors, and Dragonbane's hoard (now 23 damage) is no longer a step down. Gear drops more often, and a boss always drops a piece"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A LUTE AND A VAULT: Loras wants his lute back from a Deepwood troll, and Mirelle wants two gems for her vault's first shelf - no more paying them to move"
msgstr "A LUTE AND A VAULT: Loras wants his lute back from a Deepwood troll, and Mirelle wants two gems for her vault's first shelf - no more paying them to move"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A NAME CUT IN GOLD: PIXELHEIM in deep gold letters that catch the light, over a menu of words chosen in gold - point with the mouse or use the keys"
msgstr "A NAME CUT IN GOLD: PIXELHEIM in deep gold letters that catch the light, over a menu of words chosen in gold - point with the mouse or use the keys"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A NIGHT IN PIXELHEIM: the title opens on the village street after dark - lit windows, smoking chimneys, torches, the fountain, and the watchman on his round with his lantern"
msgstr "A NIGHT IN PIXELHEIM: the title opens on the village street after dark - lit windows, smoking chimneys, torches, the fountain, and the watchman on his round with his lantern"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A REAL VILLAGE: the dirt road from the north gate opens into a paved square held by the shrine - market pockets, scalloped corners, the old well off its SW edge - with Main Street up top and a south lane serving every door"
msgstr "A REAL VILLAGE: the dirt road from the north gate opens into a paved square held by the shrine - market pockets, scalloped corners, the old well off its SW edge - with Main Street up top and a south lane serving every door"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A SHIELD OF REEDS: Hilda has a job for you too - weave a Reedwoven Buckler at her forge, and keep it"
msgstr "A SHIELD OF REEDS: Hilda has a job for you too - weave a Reedwoven Buckler at her forge, and keep it"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A STORY TO FOLLOW: Pixelheim now has a main quest in three chapters - Under the Mountain, The Ashen Throne and The Deathless - from Sela's first job to Morvax's throne"
msgstr "A STORY TO FOLLOW: Pixelheim now has a main quest in three chapters - Under the Mountain, The Ashen Throne and The Deathless - from Sela's first job to Morvax's throne"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A TRADER IN EVERY REGION: Marta the Chandler in Saltmere, Quartermaster Brann at the Blackiron camp, Mabel the Sutler by Greyhold's road, and Gunnar's caravan on the Frostgate pass - each with their own pack and one rare piece"
msgstr "A TRADER IN EVERY REGION: Marta the Chandler in Saltmere, Quartermaster Brann at the Blackiron camp, Mabel the Sutler by Greyhold's road, and Gunnar's caravan on the Frostgate pass - each with their own pack and one rare piece"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A code-quality pass under the floorboards: one panel system instead of seven scattered flags - menus are properly modal everywhere now, and a save taken with any panel open loads clean"
msgstr "A code-quality pass under the floorboards: one panel system instead of seven scattered flags - menus are properly modal everywhere now, and a save taken with any panel open loads clean"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "A new Feats chapter in the journal: long goals - ten and thirty depths, every bounty, every mastery, a whole set worn, the whole bestiary - each bringing home a medal for the trophy shelf"
msgstr "A new Feats chapter in the journal: long goals - ten and thirty depths, every bounty, every mastery, a whole set worn, the whole bestiary - each bringing home a medal for the trophy shelf"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "AGAINST THE CLOCK: Pell's canary can't breathe the shafts' bad air for long. Once she's in your pack you have a minute to get her to Pell - the clock shows top right - or she flies back to the west gallery and you fetch her again"
msgstr "AGAINST THE CLOCK: Pell's canary can't breathe the shafts' bad air for long. Once she's in your pack you have a minute to get her to Pell - the clock shows top right - or she flies back to the west gallery and you fetch her again"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "AN HONEST BANK: Mirelle's savings now pay half a percent a day on what's in the pot, up to a tenth of it in all, and the interest is kept apart - topping up no longer folds it in or restarts the clock, so a pot can't be grown without end. The bank shows what your savings have earned so far, and there's a Deposit all"
msgstr "AN HONEST BANK: Mirelle's savings now pay half a percent a day on what's in the pot, up to a tenth of it in all, and the interest is kept apart - topping up no longer folds it in or restarts the clock, so a pot can't be grown without end. The bank shows what your savings have earned so far, and there's a Deposit all"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ARMOUR SETS: pieces of one set worn together give more - at three pieces and again at five. The bonus shows on every piece (what you wear of it, what more would give) and on the stats page"
msgstr "ARMOUR SETS: pieces of one set worn together give more - at three pieces and again at five. The bonus shows on every piece (what you wear of it, what more would give) and on the stats page"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ARMOUR TURNS ASIDE A SHARE: armour no longer subtracts a flat amount from each hit, it turns aside a share of it. More armour always helps, each point a little less than the last, and no hero is ever immune - a warrior in Blackiron at the gate takes about a third of a hit, not 1. The stat sheet shows how much of a hit of your level your DEF turns aside"
msgstr "ARMOUR TURNS ASIDE A SHARE: armour no longer subtracts a flat amount from each hit, it turns aside a share of it. More armour always helps, each point a little less than the last, and no hero is ever immune - a warrior in Blackiron at the gate takes about a third of a hit, not 1. The stat sheet shows how much of a hit of your level your DEF turns aside"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ARMS THAT WORK: each stride pumps the striding side's hand, and held gear rides it - the sword swings with the arm now, in 2D and voxel alike"
msgstr "ARMS THAT WORK: each stride pumps the striding side's hand, and held gear rides it - the sword swings with the arm now, in 2D and voxel alike"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ASKED BEFORE BIG BUYS: the house deed and the workbench ask before they take your gold - press again to buy. Furniture never blocks the doorway, an upgrade hands back what stood in its way, and new hints explain the house, deeds and the bank"
msgstr "ASKED BEFORE BIG BUYS: the house deed and the workbench ask before they take your gold - press again to buy. Furniture never blocks the doorway, an upgrade hands back what stood in its way, and new hints explain the house, deeds and the bank"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Also: the town gate moved to the north wall - no more door ping-pong when holding a key"
msgstr "Also: the town gate moved to the north wall - no more door ping-pong when holding a key"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Any stack can be dropped - one at a time, or the whole pile with Drop All"
msgstr "Any stack can be dropped - one at a time, or the whole pile with Drop All"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Audit phase two, still under the floorboards: ten panels now share one modal frame instead of hand-rolling their own - Escape, the close button and the gold line behave identically everywhere"
msgstr "Audit phase two, still under the floorboards: ten panels now share one modal frame instead of hand-rolling their own - Escape, the close button and the gold line behave identically everywhere"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "BETTER COLORIMETRY: brighter highlights and richer saturation across the heroes - vivid crimson tabards, royal blues, glowing golds, hotter rogue eyes"
msgstr "BETTER COLORIMETRY: brighter highlights and richer saturation across the heroes - vivid crimson tabards, royal blues, glowing golds, hotter rogue eyes"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "BLADES IN THEIR OWN COLOURS: Dragonbane swings red, the Obsidian Blade violet, the Blackiron Axe soot-dark, the Warden's Longsword Greyhold steel, Tidecutter sea-green - and bows and staves take their wood and stone too"
msgstr "BLADES IN THEIR OWN COLOURS: Dragonbane swings red, the Obsidian Blade violet, the Blackiron Axe soot-dark, the Warden's Longsword Greyhold steel, Tidecutter sea-green - and bows and staves take their wood and stone too"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "BUILDERS WAITING: a builder stands by every plot - talk to them and they'll tell you what it is and exactly what it still needs"
msgstr "BUILDERS WAITING: a builder stands by every plot - talk to them and they'll tell you what it is and exactly what it still needs"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Buildings grew wooden door plates - INN, SHOP and the rest hang over their doorways, readable from across the square"
msgstr "Buildings grew wooden door plates - INN, SHOP and the rest hang over their doorways, readable from across the square"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Buy the street: Odo's Emporium (2,500g), Vex's Workshop (3,500g) and Hilda's Smithy (4,000g) each sell their deed - ask the keeper behind the counter"
msgstr "Buy the street: Odo's Emporium (2,500g), Vex's Workshop (3,500g) and Hilda's Smithy (4,000g) each sell their deed - ask the keeper behind the counter"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "CALM WATERS: rivers and ponds are one clean, still, glassy surface now - no speckle, no shimmer - with the foam kept where water meets land"
msgstr "CALM WATERS: rivers and ponds are one clean, still, glassy surface now - no speckle, no shimmer - with the foam kept where water meets land"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "CAMPS IN THE WILDS: every pack lives by its own camp - a tent in its land's colours and a torch burning beside it - so you can see where trouble waits before it sees you"
msgstr "CAMPS IN THE WILDS: every pack lives by its own camp - a tent in its land's colours and a torch burning beside it - so you can see where trouble waits before it sees you"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "CITY HALL: a new slate-roofed hall stands on the south street - inside, Mayor Aldric keeps the ledger of Pixelheim's four ages: Hamlet, Village, Town, City"
msgstr "CITY HALL: a new slate-roofed hall stands on the south street - inside, Mayor Aldric keeps the ledger of Pixelheim's four ages: Hamlet, Village, Town, City"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "CLEAR ANY SLOT: the hero Continue would load can now be cleared too - X asks first, then clears them and takes you back to the title with no hero loaded"
msgstr "CLEAR ANY SLOT: the hero Continue would load can now be cleared too - X asks first, then clears them and takes you back to the title with no hero loaded"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "CONVERSATIONS LET YOU GO: E on the last line used to start the talk all over again, and Esc opened the pause menu behind it - now E reads on and closes, Esc or a step leaves at any line, and a click turns the page"
msgstr "CONVERSATIONS LET YOU GO: E on the last line used to start the talk all over again, and Esc opened the pause menu behind it - now E reads on and closes, Esc or a step leaves at any line, and a click turns the page"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "CRAFT AT HOME: fit a workbench and a small cauldron to your house shelf for 800g - smithing and alchemy, both trades, in your own four walls. The ultimate homeowner perk"
msgstr "CRAFT AT HOME: fit a workbench and a small cauldron to your house shelf for 800g - smithing and alchemy, both trades, in your own four walls. The ultimate homeowner perk"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Character customization! Pick your hero's look at creation: four palette styles per class - skin tones and outfit colors, the retro way"
msgstr "Character customization! Pick your hero's look at creation: four palette styles per class - skin tones and outfit colors, the retro way"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Chests are furniture: face one, press E, and it opens once per save - the corner finds hold gear a tier ahead of their region"
msgstr "Chests are furniture: face one, press E, and it opens once per save - the corner finds hold gear a tier ahead of their region"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Choose in the Skills menu; your title on the stat sheet carries the path. A path is for life - choose like it matters"
msgstr "Choose in the Skills menu; your title on the stat sheet carries the path. A path is for life - choose like it matters"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Crafting difficulty comes from making, never wearing - no level requirements on gear, ever (the Skyrim rule)"
msgstr "Crafting difficulty comes from making, never wearing - no level requirements on gear, ever (the Skyrim rule)"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Crafting moved to the stations: forge gear at Hilda's, brew at Vex's cauldron - the Craft tab still browses recipes anywhere and tells you where to go"
msgstr "Crafting moved to the stations: forge gear at Hilda's, brew at Vex's cauldron - the Craft tab still browses recipes anywhere and tells you where to go"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "DAWN: the survivors gather on the square, Maren reads the Crown's answer aloud, and Pixelheim decides to rebuild - with you"
msgstr "DAWN: the survivors gather on the square, Maren reads the Crown's answer aloud, and Pixelheim decides to rebuild - with you"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "DEFEAT TUCKS YOU IN PROPERLY: waking after a lost fight now puts you INSIDE the inn, at the bedside - the old wake-up tile had ended up under Odo's roof when the village was rebuilt"
msgstr "DEFEAT TUCKS YOU IN PROPERLY: waking after a lost fight now puts you INSIDE the inn, at the bedside - the old wake-up tile had ended up under Odo's roof when the village was rebuilt"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "DODGE ROLL: Shift (or L, or the right shoulder button) throws you three tiles in a blink - nothing can touch you mid-roll. Rebind it in Options"
msgstr "DODGE ROLL: Shift (or L, or the right shoulder button) throws you three tiles in a blink - nothing can touch you mid-roll. Rebind it in Options"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "DOORS ARE REAL: doorways are solid building faces now with the door set into them - walking in reads as stepping through, not sliding into a slot. Cave mouths got the same treatment in the mountainside"
msgstr "DOORS ARE REAL: doorways are solid building faces now with the door set into them - walking in reads as stepping through, not sliding into a slot. Cave mouths got the same treatment in the mountainside"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ENERGY COMES BACK: out of a fight, every hero's mana or stamina slowly returns - casters can walk to the next fight with their spells"
msgstr "ENERGY COMES BACK: out of a fight, every hero's mana or stamina slowly returns - casters can walk to the next fight with their spells"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "EVEN PIXELS: the zoom fits your window so every art pixel is a whole number of screen pixels - no more uneven columns shimmering as the world scrolls"
msgstr "EVEN PIXELS: the zoom fits your window so every art pixel is a whole number of screen pixels - no more uneven columns shimmering as the world scrolls"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "EVERY CLASS STARTS RIGHT: a new rogue carries a worn dagger that cuts with dexterity, not a strength sword - twice the bite in the first fights"
msgstr "EVERY CLASS STARTS RIGHT: a new rogue carries a worn dagger that cuts with dexterity, not a strength sword - twice the bite in the first fights"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "EVERY HELM AND BODY HAS A LOOK OF ITS OWN: Saltmere's oilskin is tarred sea-green, Blackiron soot-black with ember-hot horns, the Warden Greyhold slate with a cyan plume, Frostweave ice white, the City Plate gold on royal blue, Scaled Mail copper on dragon green, Greymaw's Hood wolf grey - and the cloaks, robes and iron each their own"
msgstr "EVERY HELM AND BODY HAS A LOOK OF ITS OWN: Saltmere's oilskin is tarred sea-green, Blackiron soot-black with ember-hot horns, the Warden Greyhold slate with a cyan plume, Frostweave ice white, the City Plate gold on royal blue, Scaled Mail copper on dragon green, Greymaw's Hood wolf grey - and the cloaks, robes and iron each their own"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "EVERY ITEM IN ITS OWN ICON: the pack and the paper doll show Shade's art for all 74 items - a rusty sword looks rusty, Dragonbane looks like a legend, and rings and amulets wear their gems"
msgstr "EVERY ITEM IN ITS OWN ICON: the pack and the paper doll show Shade's art for all 74 items - a rusty sword looks rusty, Dragonbane looks like a legend, and rings and amulets wear their gems"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "EVERY LEAD TRUE: where a material comes from now names every way there is - patches and fights in its region, the floors' patches, chests, fishing holes (Linnea's icefin comes through the ice at the Frostgate), quest rewards, the monsters that carry it, loot and the floors' hoards - the nearest first"
msgstr "EVERY LEAD TRUE: where a material comes from now names every way there is - patches and fights in its region, the floors' patches, chests, fishing holes (Linnea's icefin comes through the ice at the Frostgate), quest rewards, the monsters that carry it, loot and the floors' hoards - the nearest first"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "EVERY RECIPE WORTH MAKING: no early recipe waits on a late monster (the Beast Cleaver and the smith's gauntlets take ember shards now, not imp horns), and nothing costs more to make than it's worth. The dragon recipes are real endgame gear - Scaled Mail at 12 armour, a Grave Ward at 8, a Wyrmfang Dagger at 20 - and a Dragon Tonic brings everything back"
msgstr "EVERY RECIPE WORTH MAKING: no early recipe waits on a late monster (the Beast Cleaver and the smith's gauntlets take ember shards now, not imp horns), and nothing costs more to make than it's worth. The dragon recipes are real endgame gear - Scaled Mail at 12 armour, a Grave Ward at 8, a Wyrmfang Dagger at 20 - and a Dragon Tonic brings everything back"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "EVERY RECRUIT A STORY: the folk waiting in the wilds now each give you a small quest in the journal - help them, and they come home to Pixelheim"
msgstr "EVERY RECRUIT A STORY: the folk waiting in the wilds now each give you a small quest in the journal - help them, and they come home to Pixelheim"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "EVERY TRICK IS TOLD: the ground marks or the monster flashes first - read it, roll out"
msgstr "EVERY TRICK IS TOLD: the ground marks or the monster flashes first - read it, roll out"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Each comes with a full 12-node skill tree, its own look palette, and a proven path to the final boss - the balance sim clears the game with all seven classes"
msgstr "Each comes with a full 12-node skill tree, its own look palette, and a proven path to the final boss - the balance sim clears the game with all seven classes"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Every living thing wears a 1px outline now - heroes, villagers and monsters pop off the terrain instead of melting into it"
msgstr "Every living thing wears a 1px outline now - heroes, villagers and monsters pop off the terrain instead of melting into it"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Every piece of furniture answers to E now: the hearth crackles, the counter dreams of dinner - silence never reads as a bug again"
msgstr "Every piece of furniture answers to E now: the hearth crackles, the counter dreams of dinner - silence never reads as a bug again"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Every place has its own music now: a warm folk tune in town, old minor wanderings in the Deepwood, drowned bells over the Mirefen, a cozy lull indoors, a pulse before the dungeon plunge - and bosses get their own menace"
msgstr "Every place has its own music now: a warm folk tune in town, old minor wanderings in the Deepwood, drowned bells over the Mirefen, a cozy lull indoors, a pulse before the dungeon plunge - and bosses get their own menace"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Every spawn belongs to its terrain: ash beasts in the ash, bog things in the Mirefen - the beast you see is the beast you fight"
msgstr "Every spawn belongs to its terrain: ash beasts in the ash, bog things in the Mirefen - the beast you see is the beast you fight"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Exploration pays: 12 treasures hide across the maps - chests in the corners of the world, gold glinting on the road, an herb patch worth gathering"
msgstr "Exploration pays: 12 treasures hide across the maps - chests in the corners of the world, gold glinting on the road, an herb patch worth gathering"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "FAFNYR BREATHES FIRE: the dragon sweeps a line of flame at you and rains embers in his later fury - every attack marked on the ground first, so you can step out"
msgstr "FAFNYR BREATHES FIRE: the dragon sweeps a line of flame at you and rains embers in his later fury - every attack marked on the ground first, so you can step out"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "FESTIVAL DAYS: finish an age and Pixelheim celebrates for a day - confetti, stalls, everyone out on the square, and Barker Jory's ring toss. Land two rings of three for a prize of gold and festival pies"
msgstr "FESTIVAL DAYS: finish an age and Pixelheim celebrates for a day - confetti, stalls, everyone out on the square, and Barker Jory's ring toss. Land two rings of three for a prize of gold and festival pies"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "FINE AND EPIC GEAR HAS CHARACTER: a fine piece carries one bonus stat and an epic one two, and wears it in its name - a Fine Iron Sword of Insight, an Epic Gale Longbow of Swiftness"
msgstr "FINE AND EPIC GEAR HAS CHARACTER: a fine piece carries one bonus stat and an epic one two, and wears it in its name - a Fine Iron Sword of Insight, an Epic Gale Longbow of Swiftness"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "FISHING: stand at the end of Saltmere's jetty, by the lagoon or on the eastern rocks, face the water and press E. Fish, sea glass, the odd pearl - and the odd boot"
msgstr "FISHING: stand at the end of Saltmere's jetty, by the lagoon or on the eastern rocks, face the water and press E. Fish, sea glass, the odd pearl - and the odd boot"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "FIX: playing an empty save slot dropped a nameless warrior straight into the world, past hero creation and the Night of Ash. An empty slot now opens hero creation for that slot - Esc goes back to your saves, Begin starts the new hero from the very beginning"
msgstr "FIX: playing an empty save slot dropped a nameless warrior straight into the world, past hero creation and the Night of Ash. An empty slot now opens hero creation for that slot - Esc goes back to your saves, Begin starts the new hero from the very beginning"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "FORGET AND TRY AGAIN: in the Skills screen F forgets every skill you bought and gives the points back - 20 gold a skill, and only in the village, whose quiet lets a fighter unlearn"
msgstr "FORGET AND TRY AGAIN: in the Skills screen F forgets every skill you bought and gives the points back - 20 gold a skill, and only in the village, whose quiet lets a fighter unlearn"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "FUND THE TOWN and watch it grow: every charter is a hand-drawn redraw - lamps and market stalls at Village, a singing fountain and new roofs at Town, paved avenues and full streets at City"
msgstr "FUND THE TOWN and watch it grow: every charter is a hand-drawn redraw - lamps and market stalls at Village, a singing fountain and new roofs at Town, paved avenues and full streets at City"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "FURNITURE: Odo stocks rugs, ferns, bookshelves, banners, candelabras and benches - place them on any free floor tile you face (a Place button in the pack's new Home tab), E takes them back; your layout saves with the house"
msgstr "FURNITURE: Odo stocks rugs, ferns, bookshelves, banners, candelabras and benches - place them on any free floor tile you face (a Place button in the pack's new Home tab), E takes them back; your layout saves with the house"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Fafnyr and Morvax hit harder and last longer - bosses are events again"
msgstr "Fafnyr and Morvax hit harder and last longer - bosses are events again"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Fast travel: any waypoint you have laid eyes on is one click away - seen once, reachable forever"
msgstr "Fast travel: any waypoint you have laid eyes on is one click away - seen once, reachable forever"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Fighters run on Endurance now: Warrior and Rogue skills cost EN, and it trickles back every combat round - rhythm over potion-chugging"
msgstr "Fighters run on Endurance now: Warrior and Rogue skills cost EN, and it trickles back every combat round - rhythm over potion-chugging"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Fixed: a flaky load could leave the world pitch black until a reload - the renderer retries on its own"
msgstr "Fixed: a flaky load could leave the world pitch black until a reload - the renderer retries on its own"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Fixed: the ascension card could get stuck on screen until the next fight - it leaves politely now"
msgstr "Fixed: the ascension card could get stuck on screen until the next fight - it leaves politely now"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Fleeing and forage work exactly as before - only the surprise is gone"
msgstr "Fleeing and forage work exactly as before - only the surprise is gone"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "GLOVES, BOOTS AND SHIELDS SHOW: gauntlets colour your hands, boots your feet, and the shield you carry hangs on your off hand - a round buckler, a kite or a tower, in its own colours, in front of you or behind as you turn, put away while you draw a bow or cast"
msgstr "GLOVES, BOOTS AND SHIELDS SHOW: gauntlets colour your hands, boots your feet, and the shield you carry hangs on your off hand - a round buckler, a kite or a tower, in its own colours, in front of you or behind as you turn, put away while you draw a bow or cast"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "GO DEEPER TO GROW: clearing a floor for the first time pays XP on top of its hoard - 12 for every floor down - while monsters below your level pay 15% less for each level between you"
msgstr "GO DEEPER TO GROW: clearing a floor for the first time pays XP on top of its hoard - 12 for every floor down - while monsters below your level pay 15% less for each level between you"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "GOLD WITH A PURPOSE: from Smithing 8 Hilda forges past the cap, up to +12, each step dearer than the last and a gem a time; once Pixelheim is a city its shops sell the King's Signet, the Aegis of the Ash and the Everflask; and when every age is built the town takes commissions - the Statue of the Five (+5% XP), the Lantern Walk (+10% gold) and the Healers' Hall (potions heal a quarter more)"
msgstr "GOLD WITH A PURPOSE: from Smithing 8 Hilda forges past the cap, up to +12, each step dearer than the last and a gem a time; once Pixelheim is a city its shops sell the King's Signet, the Aegis of the Ash and the Everflask; and when every age is built the town takes commissions - the Statue of the Five (+5% XP), the Lantern Walk (+10% gold) and the Healers' Hall (potions heal a quarter more)"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "GREYHOLD: a new road leaves the east edge of the Ash Fields for Oskar's old fort on its hill - breached walls, a stone yard, his statue, and the keep where turncoats in red cloaks have made themselves at home"
msgstr "GREYHOLD: a new road leaves the east edge of the Ash Fields for Oskar's old fort on its hill - breached walls, a stone yard, his statue, and the keep where turncoats in red cloaks have made themselves at home"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Grass, roofs and stone rise out of the ground pixel by pixel - brighter pixels stand taller, so the terrain reads like a hand-carved model"
msgstr "Grass, roofs and stone rise out of the ground pixel by pixel - brighter pixels stand taller, so the terrain reads like a hand-carved model"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "HOLDINGS: the town hall's page now lists what you own - what each property has earned, what waits in its till and what a day brings"
msgstr "HOLDINGS: the town hall's page now lists what you own - what each property has earned, what waits in its till and what a day brings"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "HOUSES ARE HOUSES: every building rose again as a medieval timber home - plaster walls crossed with dark beams over stone footings, stepped hip roofs in each building's own hue, eaves, and a chimney on the ridge"
msgstr "HOUSES ARE HOUSES: every building rose again as a medieval timber home - plaster walls crossed with dark beams over stone footings, stepped hip roofs in each building's own hue, eaves, and a chimney on the ridge"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "IN THEIR OWN WORDS: the villagers ask for their quests themselves again - what they need, why, and where to look - before the quest goes in your journal"
msgstr "IN THEIR OWN WORDS: the villagers ask for their quests themselves again - what they need, why, and where to look - before the quest goes in your journal"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "INKED: every living thing's outline now seals its corners in near-black - no more dotted edges - and shadow tones deepened inside the sprites; characters pop off grass and path alike, and the voxel figures glow a touch brighter"
msgstr "INKED: every living thing's outline now seals its corners in near-black - no more dotted edges - and shadow tones deepened inside the sprites; characters pop off grass and path alike, and the voxel figures glow a touch brighter"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Inside: your own bed (free rest, forever - the inn can keep its prices) and a storage barrel"
msgstr "Inside: your own bed (free rest, forever - the inn can keep its prices) and a storage barrel"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Iva the Healer sits in the Mirefen, three marsh reeds from home - settled by the shrine, her hands heal her patron for FREE, forever"
msgstr "Iva the Healer sits in the Mirefen, three marsh reeds from home - settled by the shrine, her hands heal her patron for FREE, forever"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Jewelry grants stats while worn: +STR charms, +INT pendants, +DEX rings - and a strength charm literally helps you carry more"
msgstr "Jewelry grants stats while worn: +STR charms, +INT pendants, +DEX rings - and a strength charm literally helps you carry more"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "KEYS THAT LOOK LIKE KEYS: every key the game shows you - in a screen's footer, under a conversation, in the menu - is drawn as a raised key with a lit edge and a lip, and it dips when you press it. Pairs sit side by side (W S), choices take a slash (I / Esc), and the arrow keys show their arrows"
msgstr "KEYS THAT LOOK LIKE KEYS: every key the game shows you - in a screen's footer, under a conversation, in the menu - is drawn as a raised key with a lit edge and a lip, and it dips when you press it. Pairs sit side by side (W S), choices take a slash (I / Esc), and the arrow keys show their arrows"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "KEYS THAT TELL THE TRUTH: every key the game names is the one on your keyboard - an AZERTY board reads Z, Q and W where a QWERTY one reads W, A and Z - and follows you when you rebind"
msgstr "KEYS THAT TELL THE TRUTH: every key the game names is the one on your keyboard - an AZERTY board reads Z, Q and W where a QWERTY one reads W, A and Z - and follows you when you rebind"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "KILLS THAT COUNT: the Reach's chapters - the Saltmere coast and its sea cave, the mines and their shafts, Greyhold and its cellars, the Frostgate and its ice cave - pay nearly half again as much XP for a kill as the fields round Pixelheim"
msgstr "KILLS THAT COUNT: the Reach's chapters - the Saltmere coast and its sea cave, the mines and their shafts, Greyhold and its cellars, the Frostgate and its ice cave - pay nearly half again as much XP for a kill as the fields round Pixelheim"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "LARGE READING TEXT: everything you read at length - conversations, the story's captions, the town tour, hints, the quest line, the battle log and messages - in the big type. Long lines grow the window upward instead of running off the screen"
msgstr "LARGE READING TEXT: everything you read at length - conversations, the story's captions, the town tour, hints, the quest line, the battle log and messages - in the big type. Long lines grow the window upward instead of running off the screen"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "LIANE'S JOURNAL: ten pages lie on the floors, one per first clear, telling how five heroes of Pixelheim climbed to renew the Ember Seal fifty years ago - read them in the journal's new Story tab"
msgstr "LIANE'S JOURNAL: ten pages lie on the floors, one per first clear, telling how five heroes of Pixelheim climbed to renew the Ember Seal fifty years ago - read them in the journal's new Story tab"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "LOOT THAT FITS THE STAGE: a monster in the wilds drops what a monster of its level would, never more than its region's best - the Mirefen's skeletons no longer drop the mountain's finest blades, and the maze chest there holds a steel axe instead of an obsidian blade"
msgstr "LOOT THAT FITS THE STAGE: a monster in the wilds drops what a monster of its level would, never more than its region's best - the Mirefen's skeletons no longer drop the mountain's finest blades, and the maze chest there holds a steel axe instead of an obsidian blade"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Late-game hunting grounds: trolls and golems under the trees, ghosts and mimics in the bog - elites roam thick"
msgstr "Late-game hunting grounds: trolls and golems under the trees, ghosts and mimics in the bog - elites roam thick"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Loras the Bard sings to trees in the Deepwood, but a hamlet is beneath him - fund the Village first, pay his 150g, and his marching song sharpens your next hunt (+12% crit)"
msgstr "Loras the Bard sings to trees in the Deepwood, but a hamlet is beneath him - fund the Village first, pay his 150g, and his marching song sharpens your next hunt (+12% crit)"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Lost with a pocket full of pelts? The Craft tab now offers 'Travel to town' - one click to Pixelheim Gate"
msgstr "Lost with a pocket full of pelts? The Craft tab now offers 'Travel to town' - one click to Pixelheim Gate"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "MAREN REMEMBERS: each relic you win brings her story of its owner - Tam's stew in the snow, the five marks on the black iron, Oskar's shield and Liane's lantern"
msgstr "MAREN REMEMBERS: each relic you win brings her story of its owner - Tam's stew in the snow, the five marks on the black iron, Oskar's shield and Liane's lantern"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "MASTERY SHOWS IN THE WORK: the further your trade stands above a recipe, the likelier what you forge or weave comes out Fine - and, well past it, Epic, with the bonus stats loot has. Your own workbench at home counts as a level more"
msgstr "MASTERY SHOWS IN THE WORK: the further your trade stands above a recipe, the likelier what you forge or weave comes out Fine - and, well past it, Epic, with the bonus stats loot has. Your own workbench at home counts as a level more"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "MENUS BY TAP: every screen gets a row of buttons on a phone - the arrows, OK and Back - in the room beside the page, so it never covers what you're reading. The dock's Menu and the rows themselves answer a tap too"
msgstr "MENUS BY TAP: every screen gets a row of buttons on a phone - the arrows, OK and Back - in the room beside the page, so it never covers what you're reading. The dock's Menu and the rows themselves answer a tap too"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "MIXED PACKS: a pack in the wilds is no longer three of a kind - its leader brings company from the region, though never anything much stronger than itself"
msgstr "MIXED PACKS: a pack in the wilds is no longer three of a kind - its leader brings company from the region, though never anything much stronger than itself"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "MORE TO DO IN THE WILDS: Ana, Bram, Mira and Old Tomas have new jobs - orc raiders on the ash road, imps with a cheese knife, grave moss for the looms, walking stones in the Deepwood"
msgstr "MORE TO DO IN THE WILDS: Ana, Bram, Mira and Old Tomas have new jobs - orc raiders on the ash road, imps with a cheese knife, grave moss for the looms, walking stones in the Deepwood"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Materials weigh nothing and sell for pocket change - brew, don't hoard"
msgstr "Materials weigh nothing and sell for pocket change - brew, don't hoard"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Monster mastery! Every kill teaches: 10 slain of a family earns +5% damage against them, 25 earns +10%, 50 earns +15% - permanently"
msgstr "Monster mastery! Every kill teaches: 10 slain of a family earns +5% damage against them, 25 earns +10%, 50 earns +15% - permanently"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "NO MORE SURPRISES: a monster notices you only when it is on your screen, within five tiles and with nothing solid between you - and it shows it, with a \"!\" over its head and a hop before it charges"
msgstr "NO MORE SURPRISES: a monster notices you only when it is on your screen, within five tiles and with nothing solid between you - and it shows it, with a \"!\" over its head and a hop before it charges"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "NO TWO HOUSES ALIKE: gabled ridges on the long houses, hipped roofs on the square ones, two-story landmarks with jettied upper floors, and three timber facade styles - twin rails, cross-braces, close studs"
msgstr "NO TWO HOUSES ALIKE: gabled ridges on the long houses, hipped roofs on the square ones, two-story landmarks with jettied upper floors, and three timber facade styles - twin rails, cross-braces, close studs"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "No more ambushes. Monsters are VISIBLE in the wilds now - see them prowl, choose your fights"
msgstr "No more ambushes. Monsters are VISIBLE in the wilds now - see them prowl, choose your fights"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "OLD GEAR BACK TO THE FORGE: Hilda's new Salvage tab breaks a piece down into half of what it was made of (or ember shards), and from Smithing 8 her Reforge tab rolls a piece's rarity again - never down - with fresh bonus stats"
msgstr "OLD GEAR BACK TO THE FORGE: Hilda's new Salvage tab breaks a piece down into half of what it was made of (or ember shards), and from Smithing 8 her Reforge tab rolls a piece's rarity again - never down - with fresh bonus stats"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ONE PIXELHEIM: the old web edition has retired - this is the game now, and every hero from it still comes across from the saves screen"
msgstr "ONE PIXELHEIM: the old web edition has retired - this is the game now, and every hero from it still comes across from the saves screen"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ONE SCREEN AT A TIME: the keys go only to the screen on top. A rank-up at Morvax's fall no longer hides the throne - and the E meant for the rank-up can't choose his fate behind your back"
msgstr "ONE SCREEN AT A TIME: the keys go only to the screen on top. A rank-up at Morvax's fall no longer hides the throne - and the E meant for the rank-up can't choose his fate behind your back"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ONE STEP, ONE POSE: the stride now advances with each TILE you cross, not with the clock - four steps show four different sprites, guaranteed - and standing settles on a true neutral pose instead of a mid-stride freeze; the hop calmed down to let the footwork lead"
msgstr "ONE STEP, ONE POSE: the stride now advances with each TILE you cross, not with the clock - four steps show four different sprites, guaranteed - and standing settles on a true neutral pose instead of a mid-stride freeze; the hop calmed down to let the footwork lead"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Old heroes are seeded their role's base grit automatically - no save lost"
msgstr "Old heroes are seeded their role's base grit automatically - no save lost"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "PAST TEN: every skill tree grows two more tiers, at levels 13 and 17 - a new skill and two passives at each. Each role gains a skill that strikes every foe in reach (Cleave, Flame Wave, Fan of Knives, Holy Nova, Volley, Divine Storm, Death Cloud) and one more to finish (Rally, Arcane Lance, Garrote, Sunfire, Kill Shot, Shieldbreaker, and Drain Life, which heals you for half of what it takes)"
msgstr "PAST TEN: every skill tree grows two more tiers, at levels 13 and 17 - a new skill and two passives at each. Each role gains a skill that strikes every foe in reach (Cleave, Flame Wave, Fan of Knives, Holy Nova, Volley, Divine Storm, Death Cloud) and one more to finish (Rally, Arcane Lance, Garrote, Sunfire, Kill Shot, Shieldbreaker, and Drain Life, which heals you for half of what it takes)"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "PATCHES TO PICK: herbs, reeds, ember shards, deep roots and grave moss grow in patches around each wild region - walk over one to gather it, and it grows back after a while"
msgstr "PATCHES TO PICK: herbs, reeds, ember shards, deep roots and grave moss grow in patches around each wild region - walk over one to gather it, and it grows back after a while"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "PIXELHEIM BURNS: a new story now ends with Fafnyr setting the village alight - and a new hero starts in what's left of it"
msgstr "PIXELHEIM BURNS: a new story now ends with Fafnyr setting the village alight - and a new hero starts in what's left of it"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "PIXELHEIM MOVES TO GODOT: the game at the address you know now runs on the Godot engine - the React edition lives on as the classic edition, one click from the title, and your hero comes across from the saves screen"
msgstr "PIXELHEIM MOVES TO GODOT: the game at the address you know now runs on the Godot engine - the React edition lives on as the classic edition, one click from the title, and your hero comes across from the saves screen"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "PIXELHEIM SPEAKS FRENCH: every menu, quest, line of dialogue, item, skill, monster, the story and these notes, all 3,098 strings - choose it under Options, or the game follows your system's language"
msgstr "PIXELHEIM SPEAKS FRENCH: every menu, quest, line of dialogue, item, skill, monster, the story and these notes, all 3,098 strings - choose it under Options, or the game follows your system's language"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "PLAY ON YOUR PHONE: on a phone or tablet a thumbstick sits under your left thumb and the hero's buttons under your right - hit, roll, use and your first three skills"
msgstr "PLAY ON YOUR PHONE: on a phone or tablet a thumbstick sits under your left thumb and the hero's buttons under your right - hit, roll, use and your first three skills"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "PRICED FOR A HERO: the Village costs 800g in all, the Town 2200g, the City 2700g - instead of 2500g, 7000g and 15000g"
msgstr "PRICED FOR A HERO: the Village costs 800g in all, the Town 2200g, the City 2700g - instead of 2500g, 7000g and 15000g"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "PROPERTY THAT PAYS: a business you own now fills its till with rent every day - about a twenty-fifth of what its deed cost, a tenth more once Pixelheim is a village and a quarter more expanded - and its keeper hands you the till when you walk up to the counter. No more rent line after every kill"
msgstr "PROPERTY THAT PAYS: a business you own now fills its till with rent every day - about a twenty-fifth of what its deed cost, a tenth more once Pixelheim is a village and a quarter more expanded - and its keeper hands you the till when you walk up to the counter. No more rent line after every kill"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Paths claim the wardrobe: every path dyes your garb in its colors, deepening with each rank - a Warlord finally LOOKS like a Warlord"
msgstr "Paths claim the wardrobe: every path dyes your garb in its colors, deepening with each rank - a Warlord finally LOOKS like a Warlord"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Paths, bridges and town stay safe - stray off the road at your own risk"
msgstr "Paths, bridges and town stay safe - stray off the road at your own risk"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "People live here now - talk to them with E, Enter or Space"
msgstr "People live here now - talk to them with E, Enter or Space"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Pixelheim doubled east: new houses, a market corner, an orchard - and shops are rooms you walk into and trade by talking"
msgstr "Pixelheim doubled east: new houses, a market corner, an orchard - and shops are rooms you walk into and trade by talking"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "QUESTS on the coast: the smugglers' story and the Tidecaller for Wenna, crabs on the jetty and the lighthouse lens for Brin, your first catch for Ola, the smugglers' captain for Rook - and in Pixelheim, Pip's cat wants fresh fish"
msgstr "QUESTS on the coast: the smugglers' story and the Tidecaller for Wenna, crabs on the jetty and the lighthouse lens for Brin, your first catch for Ola, the smugglers' captain for Rook - and in Pixelheim, Pip's cat wants fresh fish"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "QUESTS! Five promises around the village: slimes for Sela, cheese for Bram (of course), wolves for Ana, a troll for the elder, herbs for Vex - talk to accept, deliver or slay, talk again to collect"
msgstr "QUESTS! Five promises around the village: slimes for Sela, cheese for Bram (of course), wolves for Ana, a troll for the elder, herbs for Vex - talk to accept, deliver or slay, talk again to collect"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "READABLE DANGER: a foe shows its level as you come near, on a small plate over its head - grey well below you, cream a match, orange a step above, red far above - so you can choose your fights before the charge"
msgstr "READABLE DANGER: a foe shows its level as you come near, on a small plate over its head - grey well below you, cream a match, orange a step above, red far above - so you can choose your fights before the charge"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "READY FOR OTHER LANGUAGES: every word the game shows - its menus, messages, quests, dialogue, items and story - can now be translated, and Options has a Language row (it follows your system's language unless you pick one). French is on its way"
msgstr "READY FOR OTHER LANGUAGES: every word the game shows - its menus, messages, quests, dialogue, items and story - can now be translated, and Options has a Language row (it follows your system's language unless you pick one). French is on its way"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "REAL WALK CYCLES: four hand-drawn frames per silhouette - legs that actually stride and bend, robes that sway, feet that lift - replacing the old sliding-feet trick, in 2D and extruded voxel alike"
msgstr "REAL WALK CYCLES: four hand-drawn frames per silhouette - legs that actually stride and bend, robes that sway, feet that lift - replacing the old sliding-feet trick, in 2D and extruded voxel alike"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "REAL-TIME FIGHTS: monsters prowl in packs and hunt you, and you swing and cast as you move - on the same numbers as ever"
msgstr "REAL-TIME FIGHTS: monsters prowl in packs and hunt you, and you swing and cast as you move - on the same numbers as ever"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "REBUILD IT: the Hamlet is four projects on the board - Odo's store, Hilda's forge, Vex's brewery, and the inn with the homes - each one cheap, and each one opens its doors again"
msgstr "REBUILD IT: the Hamlet is four projects on the board - Odo's store, Hilda's forge, Vex's brewery, and the inn with the homes - each one cheap, and each one opens its doors again"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "RETINA SHARP: the WebGL canvas was rendering at half resolution on high-density screens and getting stretched - the blur is gone, every pixel lands on a device pixel"
msgstr "RETINA SHARP: the WebGL canvas was rendering at half resolution on high-density screens and getting stretched - the blur is gone, every pixel lands on a device pixel"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "ROOMS WORTH ENTERING: plank floors and rugs, plaster walls with windows, and real furniture - beds, bread ovens, the smithy's furnace and anvils, Vex's bubbling pot, bottle cabinets, planters and trophy shields"
msgstr "ROOMS WORTH ENTERING: plank floors and rugs, plaster walls with windows, and real furniture - beds, bread ovens, the smithy's furnace and anvils, Vex's bubbling pot, bottle cabinets, planters and trophy shields"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Rank changes how you LOOK: garb brightens with every ascension and your outline turns from shadow to gold to radiant - across every class and every look"
msgstr "Rank changes how you LOOK: garb brightens with every ascension and your outline turns from shadow to gold to radiant - across every class and every look"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Rank evolution! Every 5 levels your hero ascends: Apprentice becomes Mage becomes Magus becomes ARCHMAGE - every class has its ladder"
msgstr "Rank evolution! Every 5 levels your hero ascends: Apprentice becomes Mage becomes Magus becomes ARCHMAGE - every class has its ladder"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "SAVINGS with teeth: deposit gold and it earns 2% per in-game day, up to ten days - patience pays, parking doesn't"
msgstr "SAVINGS with teeth: deposit gold and it earns 2% per in-game day, up to ten days - patience pays, parking doesn't"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "SETTLERS: three wanderers wait out in the world, each with a story and a price - meet their ask and they move into Pixelheim for good"
msgstr "SETTLERS: three wanderers wait out in the world, each with a story and a price - meet their ask and they move into Pixelheim for good"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "SHOPS FOLLOW THE STORY: Hilda's, Vex's and Odo's shelves now fill as you win the relics out in the Reach, not only as you climb the mountain - iron, staves and leather from the start, steel and better rings with each relic"
msgstr "SHOPS FOLLOW THE STORY: Hilda's, Vex's and Odo's shelves now fill as you win the relics out in the Reach, not only as you climb the mountain - iron, staves and leather from the start, steel and better rings with each relic"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "SHOPS GROW WITH THE TOWN: each new age brings Odo, Hilda and Vex more stock, and a signature item you can only buy in Pixelheim - Lamplighter's Sausages and the Lamplit Blade in the Village, a Fountain Day Roast, the Fountain Guard and a Fountain Tonic in the Town, Banquet Ribs, City Plate and a Phoenix Draught in the City"
msgstr "SHOPS GROW WITH THE TOWN: each new age brings Odo, Hilda and Vex more stock, and a signature item you can only buy in Pixelheim - Lamplighter's Sausages and the Lamplit Blade in the Village, a Fountain Day Roast, the Fountain Guard and a Fountain Tonic in the Town, Banquet Ribs, City Plate and a Phoenix Draught in the City"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "SIDE QUESTS FOLLOW THE STORY: a hub's side quests wait for its first word - Rook after Wenna's smugglers, Pell after the lost crew, Fenwick once the yard is clear, Gunnar once the wolves are gone"
msgstr "SIDE QUESTS FOLLOW THE STORY: a hub's side quests wait for its first word - Rook after Wenna's smugglers, Pell after the lost crew, Fenwick once the yard is clear, Gunnar once the wolves are gone"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "SIGNS YOU CAN READ FROM THE ROAD: a carved board hangs on chains over every door, painted with its trade - cheese, tankard, anvil, brewing pot, ledger, key - and the place's name and keeper rise as you walk up"
msgstr "SIGNS YOU CAN READ FROM THE ROAD: a carved board hangs on chains over every door, painted with its trade - cheese, tankard, anvil, brewing pot, ledger, key - and the place's name and keeper rise as you walk up"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "SKILLS WITH FACES: the dock's slots show each skill's icon - a fireball for Fireball, a shield for Shield Slam, a fist for Berserk - and poison, burns and stuns show his marks over your head"
msgstr "SKILLS WITH FACES: the dock's slots show each skill's icon - a fireball for Fireball, a shield for Shield Slam, a fist for Berserk - and poison, burns and stuns show his marks over your head"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "SOMETHING SPEAKS IN YOUR SLEEP: resting at the inn - or in Sela's tent - now and then brings a dream of the stair below, and a voice that knows your name"
msgstr "SOMETHING SPEAKS IN YOUR SLEEP: resting at the inn - or in Sela's tent - now and then brings a dream of the stair below, and a voice that knows your name"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "STAKES: some quests now end in a choice. In Greyhold, Fenwick's old crew still hides in the low cells - keep his secret or tell Ulla. On the Saltmere beach, Rook wants half the smugglers' captain's take - split it with him or give it back to the town. Each answer pays its own way, and the one who asked remembers"
msgstr "STAKES: some quests now end in a choice. In Greyhold, Fenwick's old crew still hides in the low cells - keep his secret or tell Ulla. On the Saltmere beach, Rook wants half the smugglers' captain's take - split it with him or give it back to the town. Each answer pays its own way, and the one who asked remembers"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "STRIDES YOU CAN SEE FROM THE SADDLE: the walk poses got bold - legs scissor wide on contact, a knee lifts high on the passing step, robes sway twice as far - every step on a long walk reads as a different sprite"
msgstr "STRIDES YOU CAN SEE FROM THE SADDLE: the walk poses got bold - legs scissor wide on contact, a knee lifts high on the passing step, robes sway twice as far - every step on a long walk reads as a different sprite"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "STUNS HAVE LIMITS: a stunned monster no longer casts or uses its tricks, but bosses and elites shake off a second stun for a while after the first - Frost Nova can't hold them in place"
msgstr "STUNS HAVE LIMITS: a stunned monster no longer casts or uses its tricks, but bosses and elites shake off a second stun for a while after the first - Frost Nova can't hold them in place"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Settlers move in as the town rises: Mira the Weaver, Old Tomas, Serra and Fenn each arrive with their tier - and their own things to say about you"
msgstr "Settlers move in as the town rises: Mira the Weaver, Old Tomas, Serra and Fenn each arrive with their tier - and their own things to say about you"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Shadows became a tone, not a hole: half-strength and shorter under a higher sun - the long black smears are gone"
msgstr "Shadows became a tone, not a hole: half-strength and shorter under a higher sun - the long black smears are gone"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Shingle courses laid across every roof plane - big roofs read as built, not painted"
msgstr "Shingle courses laid across every roof plane - big roofs read as built, not painted"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Shop signs are part of the building now - a proper facade with the placard hung high, no more floating planks"
msgstr "Shop signs are part of the building now - a proper facade with the placard hung high, no more floating planks"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Specializations! At your first ascension, every class faces a choice of two paths - Juggernaut or Warlord, Pyromancer or Stormcaller, Plaguelord or Bonelord... fourteen identities across the roster"
msgstr "Specializations! At your first ascension, every class faces a choice of two paths - Juggernaut or Warlord, Pyromancer or Stormcaller, Plaguelord or Bonelord... fourteen identities across the roster"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Still not a single audio file - every note is synthesized live, like the sprites"
msgstr "Still not a single audio file - every note is synthesized live, like the sprites"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Swap the rusty sword for Dragonbane and WATCH the swap - appearance is derived live from what you wear"
msgstr "Swap the rusty sword for Dragonbane and WATCH the swap - appearance is derived live from what you wear"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "TEXT YOU CAN READ: every word is now set in Pixeloid, a clear pixel type, at twice its size - the small thin print in the pack, the skills, the stats and the options is gone"
msgstr "TEXT YOU CAN READ: every word is now set in Pixeloid, a clear pixel type, at twice its size - the small thin print in the pack, the skills, the stats and the options is gone"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE AGES BUILD ON PLANNED LOTS: new cottages rise by the river walk, the barn across the bridge, lamps along Upper Street and then the gate road, and the fountain at the square's heart. A walled garden hides between the homes and the river - and someone left something in it"
msgstr "THE AGES BUILD ON PLANNED LOTS: new cottages rise by the river walk, the barn across the bridge, lamps along Upper Street and then the gate road, and the fountain at the square's heart. A walled garden hides between the homes and the river - and someone left something in it"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE ALCHEMY NOOK (Manor): two of a brew distill into a better one - health potions into greater, greater into elixirs"
msgstr "THE ALCHEMY NOOK (Manor): two of a brew distill into a better one - health potions into greater, greater into elixirs"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE BANK OPENS: Mirelle the Banker waits on the overworld road - a City charter and 500 gold of founding capital bring her ledger home, right beside the city hall"
msgstr "THE BANK OPENS: Mirelle the Banker waits on the overworld road - a City charter and 500 gold of founding capital bring her ledger home, right beside the city hall"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE BLACKIRON PLATE: helm, plate, gauntlets, sabatons and a bulwark (+STR, heavy), and the Blackiron Axe - forged at Hilda's from the seam's ore"
msgstr "THE BLACKIRON PLATE: helm, plate, gauntlets, sabatons and a bulwark (+STR, heavy), and the Blackiron Axe - forged at Hilda's from the seam's ore"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE CARAVAN: stake 500 gold on a trade run and hear the news half a day later - most return heavy with profit, some meet raiders on the road"
msgstr "THE CARAVAN: stake 500 gold on a trade run and hear the news half a day later - most return heavy with profit, some meet raiders on the road"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE CELLARS: down the keep's stair to the guardroom, the old cells, the crypt and the captain's hall, where Greyhold's dead garrison still stands watch - and the Hollow Captain keeps Oskar's Shield, the third of the five relics"
msgstr "THE CELLARS: down the keep's stair to the guardroom, the old cells, the crypt and the captain's hall, where Greyhold's dead garrison still stands watch - and the Hollow Captain keeps Oskar's Shield, the third of the five relics"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE COAST is wild: slimes, goblin smugglers and drowned skeletons keep their camps on its dunes and beaches, and sea glass washes up to gather - a new crafting material"
msgstr "THE COAST is wild: slimes, goblin smugglers and drowned skeletons keep their camps on its dunes and beaches, and sea glass washes up to gather - a new crafting material"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE DEEP HUNT: once Morvax is down, the stair behind his throne goes on into the dark. Depth after depth without end, each harder than the last, with foes from every family - wyverns beside wendigos, iron demons beside cutthroats - and an elite guarding every third depth"
msgstr "THE DEEP HUNT: once Morvax is down, the stair behind his throne goes on into the dark. Depth after depth without end, each harder than the last, with foes from every family - wyverns beside wendigos, iron demons beside cutthroats - and an elite guarding every third depth"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE DIORAMA IS THE GAME: voxel is the default renderer now - Pixelheim opens in 3D. The classic WebGL canvas and DOM tiles stay one click away in Options"
msgstr "THE DIORAMA IS THE GAME: voxel is the default renderer now - Pixelheim opens in 3D. The classic WebGL canvas and DOM tiles stay one click away in Options"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE DIORAMA SHINES: filmic color grading and a soft viewer-side fill light - your hero and every facade step out of the murk while the sun keeps doing the sculpting"
msgstr "THE DIORAMA SHINES: filmic color grading and a soft viewer-side fill light - your hero and every facade step out of the murk while the sun keeps doing the sculpting"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE DOCK: your portrait, health and energy, six skill slots and your gold now sit in one wooden dock along the bottom, with experience as a gold line across its top - the rest of the screen is the world; its Menu lists every screen with its key and lights up when points are waiting"
msgstr "THE DOCK: your portrait, health and energy, six skill slots and your gold now sit in one wooden dock along the bottom, with experience as a gold line across its top - the rest of the screen is the world; its Menu lists every screen with its key and lights up when points are waiting"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE EDGE STOPPED BEING A RECTANGLE: a stream winds down the whole east side and bulges into a pond, forest creeps past the west and south walls - the village sits in country now"
msgstr "THE EDGE STOPPED BEING A RECTANGLE: a stream winds down the whole east side and bulges into a pond, forest creeps past the west and south walls - the village sits in country now"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE ENDING SHOWS YOUR TOWN: slay Morvax and you walk home to a festival - the camera shows the Pixelheim you built, age by age, before the credits roll"
msgstr "THE ENDING SHOWS YOUR TOWN: slay Morvax and you walk home to a festival - the camera shows the Pixelheim you built, age by age, before the credits roll"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE ENDING: slaying Morvax plays the ending over the village, then the credits - starring every creature you fought, and Infinite Cheese Wheels as themselves"
msgstr "THE ENDING: slaying Morvax plays the ending over the village, then the credits - starring every creature you fought, and Infinite Cheese Wheels as themselves"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE FIRST FIELDS: a pack never hides a stronger kind than the one leading it - the slimes east of the gate come three at a time for Sela's quest, and the orc packs by the Ash road are orcs, with no wyvern among them"
msgstr "THE FIRST FIELDS: a pack never hides a stronger kind than the one leading it - the slimes east of the gate come three at a time for Sela's quest, and the orc packs by the Ash road are orcs, with no wyvern among them"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE FROSTGATE PASS: a narrow road climbs north out of the Ash Fields into snow - pines on white ridges, a frozen lake, and at the head of the pass Liane's observatory, built over the old ice cave. Up here the wind blows where the birds would sing"
msgstr "THE FROSTGATE PASS: a narrow road climbs north out of the Ash Fields into snow - pines on white ridges, a frozen lake, and at the head of the pass Liane's observatory, built over the old ice cave. Up here the wind blows where the birds would sing"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE FROSTWEAVE: hood, robe, mitts, boots and a rime orb (+INT), and the Rime Staff - woven at Vex's cauldron from frost lilies and yeti fur"
msgstr "THE FROSTWEAVE: hood, robe, mitts, boots and a rime orb (+INT), and the Rime Staff - woven at Vex's cauldron from frost lilies and yeti fur"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE GARDEN (Manor): drinks your victories and pours breakfast - every 6th win ripens into bread or cheese, turn and turn about"
msgstr "THE GARDEN (Manor): drinks your victories and pours breakfast - every 6th win ripens into bread or cheese, turn and turn about"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE GREYHOLD WARDEN: helm, hauberk, gauntlets, boots and a kite shield (+STR and +DEX), and the Warden's Longsword - forged at Hilda's from the fort's old steel"
msgstr "THE GREYHOLD WARDEN: helm, hauberk, gauntlets, boots and a kite shield (+STR and +DEX), and the Warden's Longsword - forged at Hilda's from the fort's old steel"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE HALL EARNED ITS NAME: T-shaped with a lamped forecourt, stone-footed walls, and a bell tower flying a red banner over the ridge - found by its door, not its address"
msgstr "THE HALL EARNED ITS NAME: T-shaped with a lamped forecourt, stone-footed walls, and a bell tower flying a red banner over the ridge - found by its door, not its address"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE HEROES GOT A REFONT: the warrior wears a crested visor helm, pauldrons and a war tabard; the mage a true pointed hat and a starred robe; the rogue vanishes into a deep hood with burning eyes; the cleric carries a gold-crossed mitre - and every look, rank and path variant inherits the new faces"
msgstr "THE HEROES GOT A REFONT: the warrior wears a crested visor helm, pauldrons and a war tabard; the mage a true pointed hat and a starred robe; the rogue vanishes into a deep hood with burning eyes; the cleric carries a gold-crossed mitre - and every look, rank and path variant inherits the new faces"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE HOUSE GROWS: Odo sells the bigger deeds - the COTTAGE (5,000g) opens a second room, the MANOR (12,000g) opens a wing - each with its own interior, served the moment you walk in"
msgstr "THE HOUSE GROWS: Odo sells the bigger deeds - the COTTAGE (5,000g) opens a second room, the MANOR (12,000g) opens a wing - each with its own interior, served the moment you walk in"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE ICE CAVE: down the observatory's stair, yetis, wendigos and frost mammoths in frosted galleries - and Rimefang, a white drake that breathes frost, curled up on Liane's Lantern, the fourth of the five relics"
msgstr "THE ICE CAVE: down the observatory's stair, yetis, wendigos and frost mammoths in frosted galleries - and Rimefang, a white drake that breathes frost, curled up on Liane's Lantern, the fourth of the five relics"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE KEYS YOU CHOSE: every line that names a key - the Night of Ash's steps, the hints, the journal page among the bones, the festival's ring toss - names the key you bound. The bones' page used to say J, which strikes; it now says the journal's key"
msgstr "THE KEYS YOU CHOSE: every line that names a key - the Night of Ash's steps, the hints, the journal page among the bones, the festival's ring toss - names the key you bound. The bones' page used to say J, which strikes; it now says the journal's key"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE LAST WAGON DOWN: once his strongbox is home, Gunnar asks you to walk the pass's last wagon down from the cave mouth. Old Bergit the mammoth hauls it - slowly, and she stops dead whenever anything with teeth comes near. Three ambushes wait along the road; stay close, clear them, and keep the wagon in one piece"
msgstr "THE LAST WAGON DOWN: once his strongbox is home, Gunnar asks you to walk the pass's last wagon down from the cave mouth. Old Bergit the mammoth hauls it - slowly, and she stops dead whenever anything with teeth comes near. Three ambushes wait along the road; stay close, clear them, and keep the wagon in one piece"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE LEDGER KNOWS ITS PEOPLE: the projects ledger lists who lives in town and what each brings - Iva's healing, Wren's post, Loras's song, Mirelle's bank"
msgstr "THE LEDGER KNOWS ITS PEOPLE: the projects ledger lists who lives in town and what each brings - Iva's healing, Wren's post, Loras's song, Mirelle's bank"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE MAP CHARTS WHERE YOU STAND: opening it in town shows Pixelheim's streets as you have walked them - it used to always show the overworld, a wall of fog for anyone who had not left town yet"
msgstr "THE MAP CHARTS WHERE YOU STAND: opening it in town shows Pixelheim's streets as you have walked them - it used to always show the overworld, a wall of fog for anyone who had not left town yet"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE MOUNTAIN COMES LAST: since the Night of Ash the mountain's gate is barred. Maren knows what opens it - the four relics the five climbers left in the Reach. Win them back from Saltmere, Blackiron, Greyhold and the Frostgate in any order, bring them home, and she opens the gate with the fifth: her promise"
msgstr "THE MOUNTAIN COMES LAST: since the Night of Ash the mountain's gate is barred. Maren knows what opens it - the four relics the five climbers left in the Reach. Win them back from Saltmere, Blackiron, Greyhold and the Frostgate in any order, bring them home, and she opens the gate with the fifth: her promise"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE NIGHT OF ASH TEACHES THE GAME: the first night is now a walk through everything a hero needs, one thing at a time. Ash hounds come out of the fire inside the gate - one tells a lunge to roll through; Bram is pinned under a beam on Upper Street; Sela binds your cuts and hands you a leather cap to wear from your pack; you carry water from the well on the green to three burning homes, and each fire dies as you douse it; embers swarm the square for your first skill; and Maren waits at the shrine. Hurt on the way, and the game shows you how to drink a potion"
msgstr "THE NIGHT OF ASH TEACHES THE GAME: the first night is now a walk through everything a hero needs, one thing at a time. Ash hounds come out of the fire inside the gate - one tells a lunge to roll through; Bram is pinned under a beam on Upper Street; Sela binds your cuts and hands you a leather cap to wear from your pack; you carry water from the well on the green to three burning homes, and each fire dies as you douse it; embers swarm the square for your first skill; and Maren waits at the shrine. Hurt on the way, and the game shows you how to drink a potion"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE OPENING PLAYS THROUGH: in the browser the story froze as it turned from the whispers below to the title - it now runs to the end and on to making your hero"
msgstr "THE OPENING PLAYS THROUGH: in the browser the story froze as it turned from the whispers below to the title - it now runs to the end and on to making your hero"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE OPENING: New Game now begins with the story - Pixelheim at peace, the Ashen Mountain waking with Fafnyr in its smoke, the heroes who climbed and never came back, and the whispers that rise from below"
msgstr "THE OPENING: New Game now begins with the story - Pixelheim at peace, the Ashen Mountain waking with Fafnyr in its smoke, the heroes who climbed and never came back, and the whispers that rise from below"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE PATH GRAPH: your identity is a walk, not a checkbox - every class branches at each rank: pick a path at rank I, its advanced form (or CROSS OVER to the rival's) at rank II, and a capstone identity at rank III"
msgstr "THE PATH GRAPH: your identity is a walk, not a checkbox - every class branches at each rank: pick a path at rank I, its advanced form (or CROSS OVER to the rival's) at rank II, and a capstone identity at rank III"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE REACH GROWS: a new road leaves the bottom of the marsh, down through the cliffs to SALTMERE - dunes and pines, a fishing hamlet on the beach, a lagoon, a jetty out into the sea and a cave under the western headland"
msgstr "THE REACH GROWS: a new road leaves the bottom of the marsh, down through the cliffs to SALTMERE - dunes and pines, a fishing hamlet on the beach, a lagoon, a jetty out into the sea and a cave under the western headland"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE ROOF CARNIVAL IS OVER: one weathered medieval family - oak shingle, slate, golden thatch, moss - replaces the red/purple/green patchwork, each building weathered its own way"
msgstr "THE ROOF CARNIVAL IS OVER: one weathered medieval family - oak shingle, slate, golden thatch, moss - replaces the red/purple/green patchwork, each building weathered its own way"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE RULE, SPELLED OUT: the Skills screen now says how points come - one each level, one more each rank"
msgstr "THE RULE, SPELLED OUT: the Skills screen now says how points come - one each level, one more each rank"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE SEA CAVE under the western headland: six torchlit chambers of drowned skeletons, slimes and crabs, two chests - and the Tidecaller in its grotto. It leaves Tam's Ladle, the first of the five relics"
msgstr "THE SEA CAVE under the western headland: six torchlit chambers of drowned skeletons, slimes and crabs, two chests - and the Tidecaller in its grotto. It leaves Tam's Ladle, the first of the five relics"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE SHAFTS: torchlit galleries of goblin diggers and spearmen, stone golems in the cart hall, ore veins in the dead ends - and the Seam Warden, an iron demon guarding the deep seam. It leaves the Black Ingot, the second of the five relics"
msgstr "THE SHAFTS: torchlit galleries of goblin diggers and spearmen, stone golems in the cart hall, ore veins in the dead ends - and the Seam Warden, an iron demon guarding the deep seam. It leaves the Black Ingot, the second of the five relics"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE SHELF OF HONOR (Cottage): display the Dragon Scale (+2 DEF), the Crown of the Deathless (+2 to every stat) or the Flawless Emerald (+10% shop sell price) - sell your trophies for gold, or shelve them for power"
msgstr "THE SHELF OF HONOR (Cottage): display the Dragon Scale (+2 DEF), the Crown of the Deathless (+2 to every stat) or the Flawless Emerald (+10% shop sell price) - sell your trophies for gold, or shelve them for power"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE SQUARE'S FOUNTAIN: a stone basin of clear water with a jet at its heart, where a plain old sprite used to stand - and the village well wears a little roof"
msgstr "THE SQUARE'S FOUNTAIN: a stone basin of clear water with a jet at its heart, where a plain old sprite used to stand - and the village well wears a little roof"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE STORY KNOWS: bringing a settler home, lighting the streets and setting Fafnyr's scale in the fountain join the main quest - as side steps, never in the mountain's way"
msgstr "THE STORY KNOWS: bringing a settler home, lighting the streets and setting Fafnyr's scale in the fountain join the main quest - as side steps, never in the mountain's way"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE THRONE BELOW: when Morvax falls he kneels, and you decide. Destroy him - or, if Maren told you her story of the five and you carry Liane's last page, lay him to rest"
msgstr "THE THRONE BELOW: when Morvax falls he kneels, and you decide. Destroy him - or, if Maren told you her story of the five and you carry Liane's last page, lay him to rest"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE TOWN RISES: fund a project and the camera shows you what went up the moment you're back in town - and says so when Pixelheim becomes a village, a town or a city"
msgstr "THE TOWN RISES: fund a project and the camera shows you what went up the moment you're back in town - and says so when Pixelheim becomes a village, a town or a city"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE TOWN SENDS YOU OUT: once Maren has asked for the relics, Pixelheim's folk have errands in the Reach - Hilda wants Blackiron ore, Vex wants Saltmere's sea glass, Sela has heard of the smugglers' rum, Bram needs the miners' humming cheese, Ana her father's badge from Greyhold and Mira yeti fur from the Frostgate. They pay in embers, potions, gems and cheese"
msgstr "THE TOWN SENDS YOU OUT: once Maren has asked for the relics, Pixelheim's folk have errands in the Reach - Hilda wants Blackiron ore, Vex wants Saltmere's sea glass, Sela has heard of the smugglers' rum, Bram needs the miners' humming cheese, Ana her father's badge from Greyhold and Mira yeti fur from the Frostgate. They pay in embers, potions, gems and cheese"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE TOWN TALKS: the villagers bring up your latest deed first - the floor you came back from, the boss you felled, the project you paid for, the settler who moved in"
msgstr "THE TOWN TALKS: the villagers bring up your latest deed first - the floor you came back from, the boss you felled, the project you paid for, the settler who moved in"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE TOWN, REBUILT: every house in Pixelheim is now one of Shade's medieval cottages - gabled roofs in terracotta, golden thatch, moss or slate, timber-framed walls, windows and chimneys - in every age of the town"
msgstr "THE TOWN, REBUILT: every house in Pixelheim is now one of Shade's medieval cottages - gabled roofs in terracotta, golden thatch, moss or slate, timber-framed walls, windows and chimneys - in every age of the town"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE TRUE STRIDE: the hero's legs scissor now - one swings ahead, one trails behind, split in real depth - on top of the hop and the lean"
msgstr "THE TRUE STRIDE: the hero's legs scissor now - one swings ahead, one trails behind, split in real depth - on top of the hop and the lean"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE TRUTH OF IT: Maren keeps the barred gate's words until it opens - no more talk of an open gate north of the bridge the morning after the fire - and says the next step in her own voice instead of telling you to ask her"
msgstr "THE TRUTH OF IT: Maren keeps the barred gate's words until it opens - no more talk of an open gate north of the bridge the morning after the fire - and says the next step in her own voice instead of telling you to ask her"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE VOXEL HERO WALKS FOR REAL: the same 4-beat stride as the 2D sheets - body bob, feet shuffling, gear riding every step - extruded frame by frame, with a slight lean into each stride"
msgstr "THE VOXEL HERO WALKS FOR REAL: the same 4-beat stride as the 2D sheets - body bob, feet shuffling, gear riding every step - extruded frame by frame, with a slight lean into each stride"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE WORLD DOUBLED: the Ashenreach is now 96x64 - broader ash fields, a wider river, longer roads, and mountains that take real walking to reach"
msgstr "THE WORLD DOUBLED: the Ashenreach is now 96x64 - broader ash fields, a wider river, longer roads, and mountains that take real walking to reach"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "THE WORLD GREW WILD: flower patches, standing stones and grass tufts scattered across the meadows, and the forests are full of round berry bushes - all grown from position math, no two maps alike"
msgstr "THE WORLD GREW WILD: flower patches, standing stones and grass tufts scattered across the meadows, and the forests are full of round berry bushes - all grown from position math, no two maps alike"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "TRUE EQUIPMENT LAYERS: gear is drawn into your sprite now, pixel by pixel - plate on the torso, helm on the crown, shield on the arm, blade in the hand"
msgstr "TRUE EQUIPMENT LAYERS: gear is drawn into your sprite now, pixel by pixel - plate on the torso, helm on the crown, shield on the arm, blade in the hand"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The CODEX opens from the HUD: your mastery progress bars on one tab, a bestiary on the other - monsters reveal their numbers only once you've drawn their family's blood"
msgstr "The CODEX opens from the HUD: your mastery progress bars on one tab, a bestiary on the other - monsters reveal their numbers only once you've drawn their family's blood"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The Deepwood and the Mirefen are twice as deep - forests you can actually get lost in, marshes worth a map"
msgstr "The Deepwood and the Mirefen are twice as deep - forests you can actually get lost in, marshes worth a map"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The Dragon Post: once the story is done, Fafnyr flies the furthest piece of each day's post himself - fast, warm, occasionally on fire"
msgstr "The Dragon Post: once the story is done, Fafnyr flies the furthest piece of each day's post himself - fast, warm, occasionally on fire"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The HUD's Map button speaks a proper event now instead of faking an M keypress - it keeps working even after you rebind your keys"
msgstr "The HUD's Map button speaks a proper event now instead of faking an M keypress - it keeps working even after you rebind your keys"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The Skills panel grew the full graph: nodes, ascension edges, your walked path aglow - and any missed choice can be claimed right there"
msgstr "The Skills panel grew the full graph: nodes, ascension edges, your walked path aglow - and any missed choice can be claimed right there"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The breeze is back in 3D: grass, flowers, forest and marsh sway, water shimmers - the same two-frame breath as the classic renderer"
msgstr "The breeze is back in 3D: grass, flowers, forest and marsh sway, water shimmers - the same two-frame breath as the classic renderer"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The controls moved into a legend at the side - every key at a glance, rebindable in Options"
msgstr "The controls moved into a legend at the side - every key at a glance, rebindable in Options"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The decor got real carpentry too: lamp posts with glowing lanterns, a roofed well, rail fences that connect, market stalls under striped awnings, round barrels, plank crates - and real trees in the deep woods"
msgstr "The decor got real carpentry too: lamp posts with glowing lanterns, a roofed well, rail fences that connect, market stalls under striped awnings, round barrels, plank crates - and real trees in the deep woods"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The inventory doll wears your gear live - equip a piece and watch your character change right there in the preview"
msgstr "The inventory doll wears your gear live - equip a piece and watch your character change right there in the preview"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The inventory grew a mirror: a paper doll of your hero with every worn piece laid on the body - click a piece to take it off"
msgstr "The inventory grew a mirror: a paper doll of your hero with every worn piece laid on the body - click a piece to take it off"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The pack's Craft tab knows your home station: 'You are at your own workbench - craft freely'"
msgstr "The pack's Craft tab knows your home station: 'You are at your own workbench - craft freely'"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The quest is now Relics of the Five - four to find, the five's to bring home - and the town's goals and the bounty board no longer offer floors behind a barred gate"
msgstr "The quest is now Relics of the Five - four to find, the five's to bring home - and the town's goals and the bounty board no longer offer floors behind a barred gate"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The skill tree looks like a tree: three named paths, tier badges from I to CAP, connector lines, and the numbers on every skill - multiplier, stat, cost - before you commit"
msgstr "The skill tree looks like a tree: three named paths, tier badges from I to CAP, connector lines, and the numbers on every skill - multiplier, stat, cost - before you commit"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The three renderers now share one camera, one day/night clock and one interaction-prompt rule - the classic renderer's prompt had quietly drifted; it agrees with the others again"
msgstr "The three renderers now share one camera, one day/night clock and one interaction-prompt rule - the classic renderer's prompt had quietly drifted; it agrees with the others again"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The title screen is a living diorama: three mountain ridges deep, a smoldering summit, drifting fog, and the game's own monsters parading past - watch for the dragon"
msgstr "The title screen is a living diorama: three mountain ridges deep, a smoldering summit, drifting fog, and the game's own monsters parading past - watch for the dragon"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The town signs its doors: GOODS, FORGE, BREWS, INN - no more hunting for the craft stations"
msgstr "The town signs its doors: GOODS, FORGE, BREWS, INN - no more hunting for the craft stations"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The village stopped being rectangles: shingled roof courses, rounded building corners, and chimneys with smoke wisps - form, not squares"
msgstr "The village stopped being rectangles: shingled roof courses, rounded building corners, and chimneys with smoke wisps - form, not squares"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The world map already knows the way - the fog is yours to lift"
msgstr "The world map already knows the way - the fog is yours to lift"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The world map is here: press M for the Ashenreach under fog of war - you only see what you have walked"
msgstr "The world map is here: press M for the Ashenreach under fog of war - you only see what you have walked"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "The world stopped ticking on one metronome - every villager, beast and blade of grass moves to its own beat"
msgstr "The world stopped ticking on one metronome - every villager, beast and blade of grass moves to its own beat"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Thirty wearables got hand-fitted overlays cut to the hero's anatomy - every sword, axe, bow, staff, robe, helm and shield, tiered by palette"
msgstr "Thirty wearables got hand-fitted overlays cut to the hero's anatomy - every sword, axe, bow, staff, robe, helm and shield, tiered by palette"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Three new classes! The RANGER (death at a distance, poison arrows, unmatched escapes), the PALADIN (armor outside, faith inside - hits, heals and never flinches), and the NECROMANCER (everything they touch keeps dying)"
msgstr "Three new classes! The RANGER (death at a distance, poison arrows, unmatched escapes), the PALADIN (armor outside, faith inside - hits, heals and never flinches), and the NECROMANCER (everything they touch keeps dying)"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Turning down your old web hero takes you to the title to make a new one - no more playing a stand-in that's never saved"
msgstr "Turning down your old web hero takes you to the title to make a new one - no more playing a stand-in that's never saved"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "VILLAGE PROJECTS: the town's charters are gone - each age of Pixelheim is now a handful of projects you fund one by one, with gold and a material from the wilds"
msgstr "VILLAGE PROJECTS: the town's charters are gone - each age of Pixelheim is now a handful of projects you fund one by one, with gold and a material from the wilds"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "VOXEL PIXELHEIM: a new 3D renderer in Options - the whole world extruded into a voxel diorama, every block grown from the same pixel art you already know"
msgstr "VOXEL PIXELHEIM: a new 3D renderer in Options - the whole world extruded into a voxel diorama, every block grown from the same pixel art you already know"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Veterans get their banked points retroactively. Spend wisely - no take-backs."
msgstr "Veterans get their banked points retroactively. Spend wisely - no take-backs."

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "WALK AWAY AND SEE A BACK: every hero has a drawn rear view now - helm backs, cape, hood, hat - shown whenever you head north, in 2D and voxel alike"
msgstr "WALK AWAY AND SEE A BACK: every hero has a drawn rear view now - helm backs, cape, hood, hat - shown whenever you head north, in 2D and voxel alike"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "WALKING IS SHARP AGAIN: the camera used to chase the hero a beat behind and shake them a pixel back and forth every frame - it now eases to exactly where the hero is drawn and stands on whole screen pixels"
msgstr "WALKING IS SHARP AGAIN: the camera used to chase the hero a beat behind and shake them a pixel back and forth every frame - it now eases to exactly where the hero is drawn and stands on whole screen pixels"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "WHAT TO PRESS, WHERE YOU ARE: the \"!\" over a villager, a chest or a fishing spot is now the key that does it, on the world's own pixels - and it follows your key if you rebind it. On a phone it stays a \"!\" beside the Use button"
msgstr "WHAT TO PRESS, WHERE YOU ARE: the \"!\" over a villager, a chest or a fishing spot is now the key that does it, on the world's own pixels - and it follows your key if you rebind it. On a phone it stays a \"!\" beside the Use button"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "WHAT YOU WEAR, YOU WEAR: helmets and armour now show on your hero - an iron helm's plume, the wyrm visor's gilded horns, a leather cap, plate, scaled mail, robes and cloaks"
msgstr "WHAT YOU WEAR, YOU WEAR: helmets and armour now show on your hero - an iron helm's plume, the wyrm visor's gilded horns, a leather cap, plate, scaled mail, robes and cloaks"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "WHEAT FIELDS: golden crops sway by the gate, under the hall and beside the sheep pen - a new tile, walkable, knee-deep in the voxel world"
msgstr "WHEAT FIELDS: golden crops sway by the gate, under the hall and beside the sheep pen - a new tile, walkable, knee-deep in the voxel world"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Wren the Stablemaster walks horses by the gate - two wolf pelts for saddle leather and fast travel drops you straight at Pixelheim Square, no gate queue"
msgstr "Wren the Stablemaster walks horses by the gate - two wolf pelts for saddle leather and fast travel drops you straight at Pixelheim Square, no gate queue"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "YOUR HOUSE TOO: a lamp, hanging herbs, a bread shelf, a chest and a pie table in the hut, a dining corner and kitchen as it grows - and wherever you've set your own furniture, the house makes room for it"
msgstr "YOUR HOUSE TOO: a lamp, hanging herbs, a bread shelf, a chest and a pie table in the hut, a dining corner and kitchen as it grows - and wherever you've set your own furniture, the house makes room for it"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "You can own a HOUSE. The shut door in the south of town names its price: the deed costs 1,500g - press E and it's yours"
msgstr "You can own a HOUSE. The shut door in the south of town names its price: the deed costs 1,500g - press E and it's yours"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Your gear finally shows: the equipped weapon rides your hand, the shield your arm, the helm your head - in the world, in both renderers"
msgstr "Your gear finally shows: the equipped weapon rides your hand, the shield your arm, the helm your head - in the world, in both renderers"

#: assets/data/changelog.json
msgid "Your title lives on the HUD and the stat sheet - you are not 'Lv 12 Warrior', you are a Champion"
msgstr "Your title lives on the HUD and the stat sheet - you are not 'Lv 12 Warrior', you are a Champion"

#: assets/data/combat.json
msgid "Fafnyr rears up - the air shimmers with heat!"
msgstr "Fafnyr rears up - the air shimmers with heat!"

#: assets/data/combat.json
msgid "Fafnyr's scales split with fire - the cave is burning!"
msgstr "Fafnyr's scales split with fire - the cave is burning!"

#: assets/data/combat.json
msgid "Grandmother Gulp springs open - she has seen you!"
msgstr "Grandmother Gulp springs open - she has seen you!"

#: assets/data/combat.json
msgid "Wolves out of the trees - they've smelled the wagon!"
msgstr "Wolves out of the trees - they've smelled the wagon!"

#: assets/data/economy.json
msgid "Craft at Hilda's forge - the FORGE door in town"
msgstr "Craft at Hilda's forge - the FORGE door in town"

#: assets/data/economy.json
msgid "Craft at Vex's cauldron - the BREWS door in town"
msgstr "Craft at Vex's cauldron - the BREWS door in town"

#: assets/data/economy.json
msgid "Three wagons up the pass, one wagon down. What's left is for sale - furs, glass and good steel."
msgstr "Three wagons up the pass, one wagon down. What's left is for sale - furs, glass and good steel."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "(A man lies pinned under a burning beam. You put your shoulder to it. It shifts - then rolls away.)"
msgstr "(A man lies pinned under a burning beam. You put your shoulder to it. It shifts - then rolls away.)"

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "(She doesn't look round.) Not now, whoever you are. There are still people out in this fire - see to them. I'll be here. I'm always here."
msgstr "(She doesn't look round.) Not now, whoever you are. There are still people out in this fire - see to them. I'll be here. I'm always here."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "A city deserves an anthem. I have the tune. I need the ending - Morvax's, ideally."
msgstr "A city deserves an anthem. I have the tune. I need the ending - Morvax's, ideally."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "A song before you march! There - carry that fire into the fight, it sharpens the blade's edge."
msgstr "A song before you march! There - carry that fire into the fight, it sharpens the blade's edge."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "A village that pays its own way - the mayor talks about you, you know."
msgstr "A village that pays its own way - the mayor talks about you, you know."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "Capital received. Find my ledger by the city hall - bring your idle gold."
msgstr "Capital received. Find my ledger by the city hall - bring your idle gold."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "Fast travel to the gate drops you on the square - my post runs like a dream."
msgstr "Fast travel to the gate drops you on the square - my post runs like a dream."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "Have you seen the {project}? Of course you have - you paid for it."
msgstr "Have you seen the {project}? Of course you have - you paid for it."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "Herbs, reeds, shards - I pay full price for reagents. The wilds are a garden if you survive them."
msgstr "Herbs, reeds, shards - I pay full price for reagents. The wilds are a garden if you survive them."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "Idle gold is lazy gold. Savings, a caravan, an expansion - put it to work."
msgstr "Idle gold is lazy gold. Savings, a caravan, an expansion - put it to work."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "Not me - I've more cuts than cloth already. Somebody's still out there calling. Go!"
msgstr "Not me - I've more cuts than cloth already. Somebody's still out there calling. Go!"

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "Roll up, roll up! Three rings, three pegs - land two and the prize is yours!"
msgstr "Roll up, roll up! Three rings, three pegs - land two and the prize is yours!"

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "Sing for a hamlet? Darling, no. Light some lamps first - make Pixelheim a village, then we talk."
msgstr "Sing for a hamlet? Darling, no. Light some lamps first - make Pixelheim a village, then we talk."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "Sit. Breathe. There - whole again."
msgstr "Sit. Breathe. There - whole again."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "Sit. Breathe. There - whole again. My door is always open to the town's patron."
msgstr "Sit. Breathe. There - whole again. My door is always open to the town's patron."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "The beam - you got it off - thank you. Thank you. I'm Bram. I'll live, I think. Probably."
msgstr "The beam - you got it off - thank you. Thank you. I'm Bram. I'll live, I think. Probably."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "The board on the square lists what we need to rebuild. Coin and a little from the wilds - we'll do the rest."
msgstr "The board on the square lists what we need to rebuild. Coin and a little from the wilds - we'll do the rest."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "The mayor's ledger survived. Rebuild us, and then - then we go up that mountain."
msgstr "The mayor's ledger survived. Rebuild us, and then - then we go up that mountain."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "The post runs like a dream. Fast travel drops you right at the square now - no gate queue."
msgstr "The post runs like a dream. Fast travel drops you right at the square now - no gate queue."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "Turncoats hold the yard now - the ones who sold the garrison's stores and stayed for the walls."
msgstr "Turncoats hold the yard now - the ones who sold the garrison's stores and stayed for the walls."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "Two wolf pelts for saddle leather and I will run a proper post in town - straight to the square, no gate queue."
msgstr "Two wolf pelts for saddle leather and I will run a proper post in town - straight to the square, no gate queue."

#: assets/data/npcs.json
msgid "When the fire's down, find Maren at the shrine. She's the elder - she'll want to know who you are, walking in out of it."
msgstr "When the fire's down, find Maren at the shrine. She's the elder - she'll want to know who you are, walking in out of it."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "\"The Ballad of the Cheese Club\", verse one. A wheel came down the cliff road / on a fair and salty breeze, / and the gulls cried out in Saltmere: / It is cheese! It's cheese! It's cheese! - L."
msgstr "\"The Ballad of the Cheese Club\", verse one. A wheel came down the cliff road / on a fair and salty breeze, / and the gulls cried out in Saltmere: / It is cheese! It's cheese! It's cheese! - L."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Alchemist. One jar, the saltiest. It's the same as the rest, but I picked the wave myself. Two coppers. - Marta"
msgstr "Alchemist. One jar, the saltiest. It's the same as the rest, but I picked the wave myself. Two coppers. - Marta"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Alchemist. Reeds, yes, as many as the fen will spare. In return: what do you put in a fever draught? Mine taste of boots. - Iva"
msgstr "Alchemist. Reeds, yes, as many as the fen will spare. In return: what do you put in a fever draught? Mine taste of boots. - Iva"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Alchemist. Snow, mostly. And mittens: a yeti fur and a frost lily, worked at a cauldron. Warm hands don't crush petals. Recipe enclosed. - Linnea"
msgstr "Alchemist. Snow, mostly. And mittens: a yeti fur and a frost lily, worked at a cauldron. Warm hands don't crush petals. Recipe enclosed. - Linnea"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Banker. Insure me a wagon against yetis, wolves, avalanches and Bergit stopping dead. If you dare. - Gunnar"
msgstr "Banker. Insure me a wagon against yetis, wolves, avalanches and Bergit stopping dead. If you dare. - Gunnar"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Bram. The three asked about the cheese again. I told them the club has a song now. Tam would like to be a member. Is that allowed, after fifty years? - Morvax"
msgstr "Bram. The three asked about the cheese again. I told them the club has a song now. Tam would like to be a member. Is that allowed, after fifty years? - Morvax"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Chandler. One jar of seawater, please. The saltiest you have. - Vex"
msgstr "Chandler. One jar of seawater, please. The saltiest you have. - Vex"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Cheese man. I have ranked every cheese in the Reach. Yours is second. First is the one I have not eaten yet. - F."
msgstr "Cheese man. I have ranked every cheese in the Reach. Yours is second. First is the one I have not eaten yet. - F."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Cheese man. The wheel Hilda gives me is good. It is not great. A great cheese has a crust you can hear. - F."
msgstr "Cheese man. The wheel Hilda gives me is good. It is not great. A great cheese has a crust you can hear. - F."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Dagny. I've a new man on the bellows, an old one: your Pell. The canary sends her regards, loudly. Come and see the forge. - H."
msgstr "Dagny. I've a new man on the bellows, an old one: your Pell. The canary sends her regards, loudly. Come and see the forge. - H."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Dagny. It was not a smile. Send ten more. - Hilda"
msgstr "Dagny. It was not a smile. Send ten more. - Hilda"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Dear Bram. Best cheese in Saltmere. Only cheese in Saltmere. The gulls got the rind. Send another, and a lid. - Ola"
msgstr "Dear Bram. Best cheese in Saltmere. Only cheese in Saltmere. The gulls got the rind. Send another, and a lid. - Ola"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Dear Bram. What rhymes with cheese? I have tried everything. Please write back. - Loras, a bard in some distress"
msgstr "Dear Bram. What rhymes with cheese? I have tried everything. Please write back. - Loras, a bard in some distress"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Dear Friend. Forty barrels of what? - Odo, merchant (honest)"
msgstr "Dear Friend. Forty barrels of what? - Odo, merchant (honest)"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Dear Loras. Knees. Trees. Please. Breeze. Sneeze. Also Greyhold, which doesn't rhyme, but they asked first. - Bram"
msgstr "Dear Loras. Knees. Trees. Please. Breeze. Sneeze. Also Greyhold, which doesn't rhyme, but they asked first. - Bram"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Dear Mabel and the lads. The club has a song. Verse one is enclosed. There are nine more. Loras is working on the tenth. - Bram"
msgstr "Dear Mabel and the lads. The club has a song. Verse one is enclosed. There are nine more. Loras is working on the tenth. - Bram"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Dear Mister Bard. The Cheese Club needs a song. The garrison at Greyhold asked. Can you do cheese? - Bram"
msgstr "Dear Mister Bard. The Cheese Club needs a song. The garrison at Greyhold asked. Can you do cheese? - Bram"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Dear Mister Bram. The garrison thanks the Cheese Club. Nobody threw it at anyone. The lads want to know: does the club have a song? - Mabel, and the lads"
msgstr "Dear Mister Bram. The garrison thanks the Cheese Club. Nobody threw it at anyone. The lads want to know: does the club have a song? - Mabel, and the lads"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Dear Mister Fafnyr. Enclosed: one wheel, aged a year in Blackiron's deepest shaft. Hold it to your ear. - Bram, Cheese Club (founder)"
msgstr "Dear Mister Fafnyr. Enclosed: one wheel, aged a year in Blackiron's deepest shaft. Hold it to your ear. - Bram, Cheese Club (founder)"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Dear Mister Morvax. I hear Tam liked cheese. The club sends a wheel, for him and for you. Membership is free. No refunds. - Bram"
msgstr "Dear Mister Morvax. I hear Tam liked cheese. The club sends a wheel, for him and for you. Membership is free. No refunds. - Bram"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Dear Pip. Every post house needs someone in charge of the doves. Teach them to carry the letters, not to eat them. - Elder Maren"
msgstr "Dear Pip. Every post house needs someone in charge of the doves. Teach them to carry the letters, not to eat them. - Elder Maren"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Fenwick. Greyhold is yours to keep now. Don't let it go to your head. - Sergeant Ulla"
msgstr "Fenwick. Greyhold is yours to keep now. Don't let it go to your head. - Sergeant Ulla"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Fenwick. Oskar wore the red cloak before you did, and he asked where the pay went too. They never threw him in the cells: he was too big to fit. Keep asking. - Maren"
msgstr "Fenwick. Oskar wore the red cloak before you did, and he asked where the pay went too. They never threw him in the cells: he was too big to fit. Keep asking. - Maren"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Fenwick. The bell hangs in Pixelheim's hall now, and the mayor jumps every time I ring it. I tell him it's practice. Ring something for me at Greyhold. - Brother Teo"
msgstr "Fenwick. The bell hangs in Pixelheim's hall now, and the mayor jumps every time I ring it. I tell him it's practice. Ring something for me at Greyhold. - Brother Teo"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Fenwick. Yes. It was always allowed. Carry on. - U."
msgstr "Fenwick. Yes. It was always allowed. Carry on. - U."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Fifty years of letters to catch up on, and this is the first. One a week, I've decided. - Maren"
msgstr "Fifty years of letters to catch up on, and this is the first. One a week, I've decided. - Maren"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Fish woman. Bram says your gulls eat the rind. The rind is the best part. Your gulls are right. Tell them. - F."
msgstr "Fish woman. Bram says your gulls eat the rind. The rind is the best part. Your gulls are right. Tell them. - F."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Fish woman. This cup has a fish on it. The kings took it from your village when the sea was young. I sat on it for a hundred years. It is yours. Sorry about the dent. - F."
msgstr "Fish woman. This cup has a fish on it. The kings took it from your village when the sea was young. I sat on it for a hundred years. It is yours. Sorry about the dent. - F."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Foreman. Fifty years I came down your road for iron and paid in coppers and grumbling. The grumbling wasn't about you. The coppers were nine short. Enclosed: nine coppers. - Morvax, on a bench"
msgstr "Foreman. Fifty years I came down your road for iron and paid in coppers and grumbling. The grumbling wasn't about you. The coppers were nine short. Enclosed: nine coppers. - Morvax, on a bench"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Foreman. Your shafts dug the iron that held the dragon for fifty years, and nobody ever thanked Blackiron. Thank you. Week two of fifty years. - Maren"
msgstr "Foreman. Your shafts dug the iron that held the dragon for fifty years, and nobody ever thanked Blackiron. Thank you. Week two of fifty years. - Maren"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Forty-one, then. Forty-two with the moon. And you still owe me a game of cards. - M."
msgstr "Forty-one, then. Forty-two with the moon. And you still owe me a game of cards. - M."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Forty-one. - M."
msgstr "Forty-one. - M."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Forty-one. I went and looked. It isn't the moon. There's a new lamp by the bridge. Ask your lamplighter. - Morvax"
msgstr "Forty-one. I went and looked. It isn't the moon. There's a new lamp by the bridge. Ask your lamplighter. - Morvax"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Forty-two, with the moon. Bring the cards. - M."
msgstr "Forty-two, with the moon. Bring the cards. - M."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Forty. It's the moon, you old goat. - M."
msgstr "Forty. It's the moon, you old goat. - M."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Friend. Rope does not fall off boats. Rope is what keeps things ON boats. Ten coils. Dry ones. - Odo"
msgstr "Friend. Rope does not fall off boats. Rope is what keeps things ON boats. Ten coils. Dry ones. - Odo"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Gunnar. Liane crossed your pass with a brass star and a bag of sums, and your father carried the bag and complained all the way up. She wrote it all down. He complained in very good order. - Maren"
msgstr "Gunnar. Liane crossed your pass with a brass star and a bag of sums, and your father carried the bag and complained all the way up. She wrote it all down. He complained in very good order. - Maren"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Gunnar. There's no horse that likes snow. There are horses that hate it quietly. I'm sending you two. - Wren"
msgstr "Gunnar. There's no horse that likes snow. There are horses that hate it quietly. I'm sending you two. - Wren"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Healer. They say the fen grows reeds as thick as your arm. I pay full price. - Vex"
msgstr "Healer. They say the fen grows reeds as thick as your arm. I pay full price. - Vex"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Hello, Pip. Everything likes fish, except other fish. Ask your cat. - Old Wenna"
msgstr "Hello, Pip. Everything likes fish, except other fish. Ask your cat. - Old Wenna"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Herbalist. Your frost lilies keep a spell cold. Mine wilt before they reach the gate. How? Why? What am I doing wrong? - Vex"
msgstr "Herbalist. Your frost lilies keep a spell cold. Mine wilt before they reach the gate. How? Why? What am I doing wrong? - Vex"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Lamp man. The kings took the first lamp off Pixelheim's gate. It has a house on it. It was the only light in the hoard. I looked at it a great deal. It is yours. Light it. - F."
msgstr "Lamp man. The kings took the first lamp off Pixelheim's gate. It has a house on it. It was the only light in the hoard. I looked at it a great deal. It is yours. Light it. - F."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Maren. Another of his: \"Why did the cheese climb the mountain? Because Maren said not to.\" He wrote me that one. It isn't funny. I laughed for a week. - W."
msgstr "Maren. Another of his: \"Why did the cheese climb the mountain? Because Maren said not to.\" He wrote me that one. It isn't funny. I laughed for a week. - W."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Maren. Father swore that bag was heavier than Bergit. Was it sums or stones? - Gunnar"
msgstr "Maren. Father swore that bag was heavier than Bergit. Was it sums or stones? - Gunnar"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Maren. The weather here is wet. It has been wet for fifty years. Tam would have made a joke about it. I can't think of one either. - Wenna"
msgstr "Maren. The weather here is wet. It has been wet for fifty years. Tam would have made a joke about it. I can't think of one either. - Wenna"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Master Gunnar. Three wagons up, one wagon down. Have you thought about insurance? A gentle reminder: interest. - M."
msgstr "Master Gunnar. Three wagons up, one wagon down. Have you thought about insurance? A gentle reminder: interest. - M."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Master Rook. Gold in a cave earns nothing. Gold in my vault earns interest. No questions asked. Some questions asked. A gentle reminder: interest. - M."
msgstr "Master Rook. Gold in a cave earns nothing. Gold in my vault earns interest. No questions asked. Some questions asked. A gentle reminder: interest. - M."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Mayor Aldric. A gentle reminder: interest. - Mirelle"
msgstr "Mayor Aldric. A gentle reminder: interest. - Mirelle"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Merchant Odo. Your strongbox is under the counter, behind the third barrel. Everyone knows. A gentle reminder: interest. - M."
msgstr "Merchant Odo. Your strongbox is under the counter, behind the third barrel. Everyone knows. A gentle reminder: interest. - M."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Merchant. I have forty barrels of something. You have a shop. Let's talk. - A friend"
msgstr "Merchant. I have forty barrels of something. You have a shop. Let's talk. - A friend"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Merchant. Rope. Very good rope, a little wet. It fell off a boat. - Your friend in Saltmere"
msgstr "Merchant. Rope. Very good rope, a little wet. It fell off a boat. - Your friend in Saltmere"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Merchant. Ten coils, dry-ish. The cask is a present. Don't open it near a candle. Pleasure doing honest business. - Rook"
msgstr "Merchant. Ten coils, dry-ish. The cask is a present. Don't open it near a candle. Pleasure doing honest business. - Rook"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Miner man. A lamp with a pick on it. Gold is a stupid metal for a lamp. Kings are stupid. It is yours. - F."
msgstr "Miner man. A lamp with a pick on it. Gold is a stupid metal for a lamp. Kings are stupid. It is yours. - F."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Mister Pell. A pot with no salt in it at all, tonight at six. Bring the bird. She can say it to my face. - W."
msgstr "Mister Pell. A pot with no salt in it at all, tonight at six. Bring the bird. She can say it to my face. - W."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Mister Pell. Your canary sang all night under my window. Every song she knows, twice. - W."
msgstr "Mister Pell. Your canary sang all night under my window. Every song she knows, twice. - W."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Mistress Wenna. A question from the inn's kitchen: how much salt goes in Tam's stew? I'd like to get it right before you taste it. - Sela"
msgstr "Mistress Wenna. A question from the inn's kitchen: how much salt goes in Tam's stew? I'd like to get it right before you taste it. - Sela"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Mistress Wenna. She bit Morvax twice, and Maren once, by mistake. That was this one's great-great-grandmother. This one bites too. It runs in the family. - Pell"
msgstr "Mistress Wenna. She bit Morvax twice, and Maren once, by mistake. That was this one's great-great-grandmother. This one bites too. It runs in the family. - Pell"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Mistress Wenna. The canary finds your stew too salty. The canary has never been wrong. - P."
msgstr "Mistress Wenna. The canary finds your stew too salty. The canary has never been wrong. - P."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Morvax. Coal, a good draught, and a cheese wheel a day for the lump on my roof. Light yours. Bring a horseshoe down on festival day and we'll see whose forge is hotter. - Hilda"
msgstr "Morvax. Coal, a good draught, and a cheese wheel a day for the lump on my roof. Light yours. Bring a horseshoe down on festival day and we'll see whose forge is hotter. - Hilda"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Morvax. Nine coppers received. Fifty years of interest owing: one visit, and you stand the first round. - Garrick"
msgstr "Morvax. Nine coppers received. Fifty years of interest owing: one visit, and you stand the first round. - Garrick"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Morvax. Tam's stew, the way he made it. If you salt it before you taste it, I will hear about it. - Wenna"
msgstr "Morvax. Tam's stew, the way he made it. If you salt it before you taste it, I will hear about it. - Wenna"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Pip. My riders thank you for the doves on their hats. They don't, but they would if they were nicer. One Steve rode all the way to Saltmere on Turnip's head. - Wren"
msgstr "Pip. My riders thank you for the doves on their hats. They don't, but they would if they were nicer. One Steve rode all the way to Saltmere on Turnip's head. - Wren"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Quartermaster. You pay in iron. Iron rusts. Gold grows. A gentle reminder: interest. - M."
msgstr "Quartermaster. You pay in iron. Iron rusts. Gold grows. A gentle reminder: interest. - M."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Sergeant. Report, day forty. Water: fetched. Helmet: rung. A lad from the valley asked to join the garrison. I said yes. Was that allowed? - Fenwick (in charge, with one soldier)"
msgstr "Sergeant. Report, day forty. Water: fetched. Helmet: rung. A lad from the valley asked to join the garrison. I said yes. Was that allowed? - Fenwick (in charge, with one soldier)"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Sergeant. Report, day one. Water: fetched. Mabel: selling. Turncoats: gone. Morale: good. Me: in charge. - Fenwick (in charge)"
msgstr "Sergeant. Report, day one. Water: fetched. Mabel: selling. Turncoats: gone. Morale: good. Me: in charge. - Fenwick (in charge)"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Small human. Fish: acceptable. Cat: suspicious. Do not send the cat. - F."
msgstr "Small human. Fish: acceptable. Cat: suspicious. Do not send the cat. - F."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Small human. The cat sleeps on my tail. It is warm. I have decided to allow it. Do not tell the cat. - F."
msgstr "Small human. The cat sleeps on my tail. It is warm. I have decided to allow it. Do not tell the cat. - F."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Small one. Fafnyr says you write to him. When he flies up here he tells the three what you wrote. Tam laughs at the cat every time. - Morvax"
msgstr "Small one. Fafnyr says you write to him. When he flies up here he tells the three what you wrote. Tam laughs at the cat every time. - Morvax"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Smith. Eight horseshoes, please. On account. - Wren"
msgstr "Smith. Eight horseshoes, please. On account. - Wren"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Smith. Festival day. Have the forge hot and your face ready. - D."
msgstr "Smith. Festival day. Have the forge hot and your face ready. - D."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Smith. Ten lumps. Garrick says that's a cartload, and a cartload costs. I told him you smile once a year. He said worth it. - D."
msgstr "Smith. Ten lumps. Garrick says that's a cartload, and a cartload costs. I told him you smile once a year. He said worth it. - D."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Smith. That's Blackiron ore, the real thing. Smile if you like it. Nobody's looking. - Dagny"
msgstr "Smith. That's Blackiron ore, the real thing. Smile if you like it. Nobody's looking. - Dagny"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Smith. They say your forge is the warmest in the Reach. Mine has been cold for fifty years. What do you burn? - Morvax, the old forge"
msgstr "Smith. They say your forge is the warmest in the Reach. Mine has been cold for fifty years. What do you burn? - Morvax, the old forge"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Snow man. A bell with a snowflake on it. It rang every time I turned over, for a hundred years. I do not want it. You want it. - F."
msgstr "Snow man. A bell with a snowflake on it. It rang every time I turned over, for a hundred years. I do not want it. You want it. - F."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Soldier woman. Hard cheese is not for throwing. It is for keeping under a wing until it is warm. Then it is perfect. - F."
msgstr "Soldier woman. Hard cheese is not for throwing. It is for keeping under a wing until it is warm. Then it is perfect. - F."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "To Old Pell, who had the canary. Maren's courier says you're still alive, and so is the bird. Tam wrote me once that she bit Morvax. Is it true? - Wenna, Tam's sister"
msgstr "To Old Pell, who had the canary. Maren's courier says you're still alive, and so is the bird. Tam wrote me once that she bit Morvax. Is it true? - Wenna, Tam's sister"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "To the stablemaster. I need a horse that likes snow. - Gunnar"
msgstr "To the stablemaster. I need a horse that likes snow. - Gunnar"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Water man. A flag with a tower on it. I did not sit on this one. It was too thin. I used it to wipe my nose. Only twice. It is yours. - F."
msgstr "Water man. A flag with a tower on it. I did not sit on this one. It was too thin. I used it to wipe my nose. Only twice. It is yours. - F."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Wenna. Fifty years I've wanted to write to you, and now I can't think of a thing to say. How is the weather? - Maren"
msgstr "Wenna. Fifty years I've wanted to write to you, and now I can't think of a thing to say. How is the weather? - Maren"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Wenna. His joke about the weather: \"It isn't raining. The sea's just visiting.\" He told it every time. Every single time. - M."
msgstr "Wenna. His joke about the weather: \"It isn't raining. The sea's just visiting.\" He told it every time. Every single time. - M."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Wenna. Now you're across the square, I've nothing left to write. Come and argue about salt instead. - M."
msgstr "Wenna. Now you're across the square, I've nothing left to write. Come and argue about salt instead. - M."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Wenna. Tam told me your stew could raise the dead. I was too proud to come down and try it. I'm on the bench by the fountain now. Twelve steps from your door. I counted. - Morvax"
msgstr "Wenna. Tam told me your stew could raise the dead. I was too proud to come down and try it. I'm on the bench by the fountain now. Twelve steps from your door. I counted. - Morvax"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Wenna. That's the Reach caught up, nearly. Fifty years, a letter a week, and I still haven't told anyone what Tam did with the goat. Come over and I'll tell you. - M."
msgstr "Wenna. That's the Reach caught up, nearly. Fifty years, a letter a week, and I still haven't told anyone what Tam did with the goat. Come over and I'll tell you. - M."

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Wren. Eight shoes for eight apples. An apple a shoe. The horses can pay. - Hilda"
msgstr "Wren. Eight shoes for eight apples. An apple a shoe. The horses can pay. - Hilda"

#: assets/data/post.json
msgid "Wren. The quiet ones came. One of them ate a yeti's mitten. The yeti is upset. The horse is not. - G."
msgstr "Wren. The quiet ones came. One of them ate a yeti's mitten. The yeti is upset. The horse is not. - G."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "(He knows the hand before he breaks the seal, and reads it aloud, slowly, as if it might change.) \"Come home, you proud old goat. Nobody's angry. I'm angry, but come home anyway. The stew's on. - M.\""
msgstr "(He knows the hand before he breaks the seal, and reads it aloud, slowly, as if it might change.) \"Come home, you proud old goat. Nobody's angry. I'm angry, but come home anyway. The stew's on. - M.\""

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "A vault with something in it is a bank. Find my ledger by the hall - bring your idle gold."
msgstr "A vault with something in it is a bank. Find my ledger by the hall - bring your idle gold."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Black iron, stamped with five marks - the same seam the Ember Seal was poured from. That ingot's theirs as much as ours. Keep it."
msgstr "Black iron, stamped with five marks - the same seam the Ember Seal was poured from. That ingot's theirs as much as ours. Keep it."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Come home, you proud old goat. Nobody's angry. I'm angry, but come home anyway. The stew's on. - M."
msgstr "Come home, you proud old goat. Nobody's angry. I'm angry, but come home anyway. The stew's on. - M."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Fafnyr rears up over the square - the air shimmers with heat!"
msgstr "Fafnyr rears up over the square - the air shimmers with heat!"

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Fafnyr's scales split with fire - the roofs smoke and the cobbles crack!"
msgstr "Fafnyr's scales split with fire - the roofs smoke and the cobbles crack!"

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Feel the weight of that. I'll make something worth it - and take these embers, I've no use for fire I didn't light."
msgstr "Feel the weight of that. I'll make something worth it - and take these embers, I've no use for fire I didn't light."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Five of the red cloaks, and the yard's ours again. The gate's round the south side - or climb a breach, if you're nimble."
msgstr "Five of the red cloaks, and the yard's ours again. The gate's round the south side - or climb a breach, if you're nimble."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Four of them. They grow where the snow lies thick - and in the cave, where it never melts. I'll see they get to Vex."
msgstr "Four of them. They grow where the snow lies thick - and in the cave, where it never melts. I'll see they get to Vex."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Give his shield to whoever brings you this, and stand down. Your watch is over. - Maren"
msgstr "Give his shield to whoever brings you this, and stand down. Your watch is over. - Maren"

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Good. Now - you didn't climb up here for wolves. You want Liane's observatory. The way down to the ice cave is through her door, and something has moved in."
msgstr "Good. Now - you didn't climb up here for wolves. You want Liane's observatory. The way down to the ice cave is through her door, and something has moved in."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Gunnar's last wagon waits at the cave mouth. Walk it down the pass to his camp - the wolves know a wagon when they smell one."
msgstr "Gunnar's last wagon waits at the cave mouth. Walk it down the pass to his camp - the wolves know a wagon when they smell one."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Ha! Saltmere breathes easier. And so do I. Here's your share - fair's fair."
msgstr "Ha! Saltmere breathes easier. And so do I. Here's your share - fair's fair."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Half for you, half for me - or we hand it back to Saltmere and I go honest. Your call, hero."
msgstr "Half for you, half for me - or we hand it back to Saltmere and I go honest. Your call, hero."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "He'll come home with his ears. Thank you. Take a lily - they only bloom up here."
msgstr "He'll come home with his ears. Thank you. Take a lily - they only bloom up here."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Heavy, true, and it fits my thick head. Take this - we found it in the seam."
msgstr "Heavy, true, and it fits my thick head. Take this - we found it in the seam."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "I sent his things home on a fishing boat. I couldn't write the rest. I'm sorry. - Maren"
msgstr "I sent his things home on a fishing boat. I couldn't write the rest. I'm sorry. - Maren"

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "It does hum! Oh, it's perfect. A wheel of my own for your trouble - a fair trade between cheese people."
msgstr "It does hum! Oh, it's perfect. A wheel of my own for your trouble - a fair trade between cheese people."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Leather enough! The post stands by the north road - the square is a whistle away now."
msgstr "Leather enough! The post stands by the north road - the square is a whistle away now."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Look how it catches the light. My potions will be the envy of the Reach. Here - the first of the clear ones."
msgstr "Look how it catches the light. My potions will be the envy of the Reach. Here - the first of the clear ones."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Lovely. Vex will be insufferable about these. Keep a few for yourself - she can weave them into cloth, if you ask nicely."
msgstr "Lovely. Vex will be insufferable about these. Keep a few for yourself - she can weave them into cloth, if you ask nicely."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Mirelle will open a bank in Pixelheim - once its vault holds something worth guarding."
msgstr "Mirelle will open a bank in Pixelheim - once its vault holds something worth guarding."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "My sister's locket. They took it when they threw me in the cells - the end cell, under the straw."
msgstr "My sister's locket. They took it when they threw me in the cells - the end cell, under the straw."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "No knife? Doesn't matter. The principle of the thing. Here - and a wedge of the good stuff, later."
msgstr "No knife? Doesn't matter. The principle of the thing. Here - and a wedge of the good stuff, later."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Not bad for a first brew. Here - the good stuff, brewed proper."
msgstr "Not bad for a first brew. Here - the good stuff, brewed proper."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Now that's a coat. Here - a pearl from the jetty. Make something sharp with it."
msgstr "Now that's a coat. Here - a pearl from the jetty. Make something sharp with it."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Old Bergit pulls it - she's slow, and she stops dead if anything with teeth comes near. Stay close, clear the road, and she'll get there."
msgstr "Old Bergit pulls it - she's slow, and she stops dead if anything with teeth comes near. Stay close, clear the road, and she'll get there."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Old Pell's canary is lost in the shafts - and the air down there is bad. Bring her up quick."
msgstr "Old Pell's canary is lost in the shafts - and the air down there is bad. Bring her up quick."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Old steel - the garrison's broken blades. It's all over the yard and the cellars, if you look."
msgstr "Old steel - the garrison's broken blades. It's all over the yard and the cellars, if you look."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Real, and terrible, and the regulars will love it. Your drinks are on the house. Well - the first one."
msgstr "Real, and terrible, and the regulars will love it. Your drinks are on the house. Well - the first one."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Reeds enough to start with. Find me by the shrine - and come to me before you climb."
msgstr "Reeds enough to start with. Find me by the shrine - and come to me before you climb."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Rook wants the smugglers' captain gone - and his take."
msgstr "Rook wants the smugglers' captain gone - and his take."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Sela keeps the inn - or a tent on the square, if that's all there is. She always has a job going."
msgstr "Sela keeps the inn - or a tent on the square, if that's all there is. She always has a job going."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Smells awful. Spins beautifully. Here - a little something from my stores while I get weaving."
msgstr "Smells awful. Spins beautifully. Here - a little something from my stores while I get weaving."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Someone has. Open it, give them her things, and go and sit in the sun. - Maren"
msgstr "Someone has. Open it, give them her things, and go and sit in the sun. - Maren"

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Something in the sea cave keeps what the tide brings in - maybe Tam's things too."
msgstr "Something in the sea cave keeps what the tide brings in - maybe Tam's things too."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Sorry about the cage. I sat on it. Your bird was right to be cross. - Maren"
msgstr "Sorry about the cage. I sat on it. Your bird was right to be cross. - Maren"

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Still locked! The yetis must have given up on it. Here - your share, and then some."
msgstr "Still locked! The yetis must have given up on it. Here - your share, and then some."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "That green! The whole valley will want it. Take an antidote - the fen leaves a taste."
msgstr "That green! The whole valley will want it. Take an antidote - the fen leaves a taste."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "That's hers. That's... thank you. Here - it's not much. It's all the turncoats didn't find."
msgstr "That's hers. That's... thank you. Here - it's not much. It's all the turncoats didn't find."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "That's his ladle. That's Tam's. He stirred soup with it and conducted the whole tavern with it after. Keep it - Maren will know what it means."
msgstr "That's his ladle. That's Tam's. He stirred soup with it and conducted the whole tavern with it after. Keep it - Maren will know what it means."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "The canary stops singing. She squeezes out between the bars and flies back down to the west gallery to catch her breath - fetch her again."
msgstr "The canary stops singing. She squeezes out between the bars and flies back down to the west gallery to catch her breath - fetch her again."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "The cave mouth is under the western headland, past the lagoon. Mind the steps - and come back."
msgstr "The cave mouth is under the western headland, past the lagoon. Mind the steps - and come back."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "The gate's been barred since the fire. Sit a moment, courier - I'll tell you why, and what opens it."
msgstr "The gate's been barred since the fire. Sit a moment, courier - I'll tell you why, and what opens it."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "The last of the fires you can reach is out. The square is glowing - embers, blown off the roofs."
msgstr "The last of the fires you can reach is out. The square is glowing - embers, blown off the roofs."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "The mountain's gate has been barred since the fire. Maren knows why, and what opens it - ask her."
msgstr "The mountain's gate has been barred since the fire. Maren knows why, and what opens it - ask her."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "The stores thank you. So does my nose. Here - you've earned it."
msgstr "The stores thank you. So does my nose. Here - you've earned it."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "There's my girl! Cross as ever. Thank you - the air's safe to breathe as long as she's singing."
msgstr "There's my girl! Cross as ever. Thank you - the air's safe to breathe as long as she's singing."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "There's something else. Five of my old crew still hide in the low cells. They sold nothing - they only ran. If Ulla finds them, they hang. Will you tell her?"
msgstr "There's something else. Five of my old crew still hide in the low cells. They sold nothing - they only ran. If Ulla finds them, they hang. Will you tell her?"

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "They're out - dusty, hungry, alive. And they say the deep seam is open again, and something is guarding it."
msgstr "They're out - dusty, hungry, alive. And they say the deep seam is open again, and something is guarding it."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Three fresh fish, please! Saltmere's down the cliffs, south of the marsh - follow the path out of the reeds. Mind the crabs."
msgstr "Three fresh fish, please! Saltmere's down the cliffs, south of the marsh - follow the path out of the reeds. Mind the crabs."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Three marsh reeds, woven tight, at my forge. Make me a buckler and keep it - it's yours."
msgstr "Three marsh reeds, woven tight, at my forge. Make me a buckler and keep it - it's yours."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Through her door and down the stair, three floors down to the glass hall. Her lantern's there - the last thing she lit before the climb. Mind the cold it breathes."
msgstr "Through her door and down the stair, three floors down to the glass hall. Her lantern's there - the last thing she lit before the climb. Mind the cold it breathes."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Two fish - your own, mind. The end of the jetty is the easy spot."
msgstr "Two fish - your own, mind. The end of the jetty is the easy spot."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Two wolf pelts for saddle leather. The wolves den in the fields east of here - mind their teeth."
msgstr "Two wolf pelts for saddle leather. The wolves den in the fields east of here - mind their teeth."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Vex will show you the cauldron - at her stall on the square, or behind the BREWS door once it stands again. Potions you brew cost you a herb, not a fortune."
msgstr "Vex will show you the cauldron - at her stall on the square, or behind the BREWS door once it stands again. Potions you brew cost you a herb, not a fortune."

#: assets/data/progression.json
msgid "Wings like sails, fire like - no, don't tell me. I'll find the word."
msgstr "Wings like sails, fire like - no, don't tell me. I'll find the word."

#: assets/data/story.json
msgid "Tam's ladle. Gods. He cooked for us all the way up - stew on a mountain, in the snow."
msgstr "Tam's ladle. Gods. He cooked for us all the way up - stew on a mountain, in the snow."

#: assets/data/town.json
msgid "The bells ring as you walk in. Pixelheim knows what fell on the mountain - and Bram has been telling everyone he always knew."
msgstr "The bells ring as you walk in. Pixelheim knows what fell on the mountain - and Bram has been telling everyone he always knew."

#: scripts/elite_brain.gd
msgid "%s howls - the forest answers!"
msgstr "%s howls - the forest answers!"

#: scripts/inventory_screen.gd
msgid "%s - click to take off"
msgstr "%s - click to take off"

#: scripts/journal_screen.gd
msgid "%s - %s"
msgstr "%s - %s"

#: scripts/journal_screen.gd
msgid "Maren's letters - %d of %d delivered"
msgstr "Maren's letters - %d of %d delivered"

#: scripts/skills_screen.gd
msgid "%s: %s  Signature: %s - %s"
msgstr "%s: %s  Signature: %s - %s"

#: scripts/skills_screen.gd
msgid "Not on the dock - press 1-6 to put it on that key."
msgstr "Not on the dock - press 1-6 to put it on that key."

#: scripts/skills_screen.gd
msgid "On key %d - press 1-6 to move it."
msgstr "On key %d - press 1-6 to move it."

#: scripts/state/holdings.gd
msgid "%s: built - and Pixelheim is a %s now."
